 30 km band and 5 km peak are different definitions at R13, not two occupations, a physical variability range, or numerical error.","geographic_scope":"GOGP99 section R13 near the Strait of Hormuz. No section endpoints or current-axis coordinates extracted.","section_geometry":null,"section_orientation":"Source geostrophic velocity normal to R13; no geographic paired edge reconstruction.","layer":"Subsurface outflow description; 30 m velocity reference and 45 m transport partition do not define the width measurement layer.","time_convention":"October-November1999 GOGP99 section context. Width prose names R13 without realization suffix; R13b method/figure linkage does not supply an independently verified exact width date.","boundary_rule":"Author-described narrow faster peak near 0.4 m/s; the speed is a description, not an extracted boundary threshold.","source_url":"https://archimer.ifremer.fr/doc/00000/390/83.pdf","source_citation":"Pous, S.P., Carton, X. and Lazure, P. (2004), Hydrology and circulation in the Strait of Hormuz and the Gulf of Oman: Results from the GOGP99 Experiment, parts 1 and 2, JGR Oceans 109, doi:10.1029/2003JC002145 and doi:10.1029/2003JC002146. Institutional author versions.","source_locator":"Part2 author version printed p6/PDF7, R13 velocity-width description; part1 printed p5/PDF6 and Fig9 printed p22/PDF23, reference method; Table1 printed p13/PDF14, occupation context.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-14","source_evidence_kind":"author_reported_companion_study_geostrophic_spatial_scale","extraction_method":"Transcribed explicit width descriptions from original part2; checked companion part1 method, Fig9 and occupation table. No curve digitization.","whole_current_representative":false,"width_rank_eligible":false,"full_width_inference_eligible":false,"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"seasonal_playback_eligible":false,"is_confidence_interval":false,"phase_label":"R13 faster geostrophic peak description","phase_kind":"regional_summary","ob