t width occupation, fixed layer, geographic edges and width error unknown. The band/peak and salinity-core widths are separate definitions.","comparison_figure":"figures/persian-gulf-gogp99-geostrophic-scales.svg","comparison_figure_label":"Compare the flow band and faster peak","audit_file":"research/persian-gulf-gogp99-geostrophic-scales-scope-audit.json","audit_sha256":"6f4a7c211cb02fc5906c5d6e98279022bec688f446a1ba20aa7aa79a6c2d28d1","audit_pointer":"/measurements/1"}},{"id":"atlantic-seuc-molinari-1981-core-width","current_id":"atlantic-south-equatorial-undercurrent","name":"Atlantic South Equatorial Undercurrent","status":"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical","measurement_type":"published_regional_summary","width_metric":"author_reported_velocity_contour_core_span","approximate_width_km":120,"width_range_km":null,"range_interpretation":"One approximate author-reported 20 cm/s core width. Abstract approximately 100 km is separate unreconciled context, not an endpoint, error or independent occupation.","geographic_scope":"Eastern and western Atlantic sections: approximately 25–29 W and 4 W, within the 1978–1980 study. Not the newer 35 W ledger section or the entire current.","section_geometry":null,"section_orientation":"Source cross-current sections; no geographic edge pair or exact flow-normal projection extracted.","layer":"Subthermocline 20 cm/s isotach core. Reported core depths and vertical extent are context, not fixed width-layer limits.","time_convention":"Author summary across six 1978–1980 cruises. Individual figure dates do not date this characteristic width; no per-cruise or seasonal width series extracted.","boundary_rule":"Source defines the core as flow within the 20 cm/s isotach and reports about 120 km core width. This is not the net-flow boundary.","source_url":"https://archimer.ifremer.fr/doc/00121/23229/21063.pdf","source_citation":"Molinari, R. L., Voituriez, B., and Duncan, P. (1981), Observations in the subthermocline undercurrent of the Equatorial South Atlantic Ocean: 1978–1980, Oceanologica Acta 4(4), 451–456.","source_locator":"Printed p453/PDF p3, core definition and width paragraphs; abstract p451/PDF p1; methods/captions p452/PDF p2; net-flow boundary limitation p456/PDF p6.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-14","source_evidence_kind":"published_original_campaign_core_summary","extraction_method":"Transcribed the explicit contour-defined body core width after original-page review; no figure digitization or geographic edge inference.","whole_current_representative":false,"width_rank_eligible":false,"full_width_inference_eligible":false,"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"seasonal_playback_eligible":false,"is_confidence_interval":false,"phase_label":"1978–1980 study · 20 cm/s core summary","phase_kind":"regional_summary","observed_period":null,"calendar_months":null,"fixed_layer_bounds_m":null,"uncertainty_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"source_quality_note":"Body about 120 km versus abstract about 100 km retained separately. Reference captions use 1000 db while prose uses 1000 m. Numerical width uncertainty and net-flow boundaries unknown.","remaining_gates":["Resolve source approximate-width description discrepancy without manufacturing a range.","Recover paired geographic edges and compatible repeated sections before mapping or annual variability.","Independent scientific admission."],"original_regional_context":{"description_kind":"atlantic_seuc_contour_core_summary","core_threshold_cm_s":20,"abstract_description_width_km":100,"body_core_width_km":120,"abstract_body_discrepancy_reconciled":false,"descriptions_are_independent_occupations":false,"descriptions_define_range_or_error":false,"geostrophic_reference_prose":"1000 m","geostrophic_reference_figure_captions":"1000 db","pressure_depth_expressions_are_exact_conversion":false,"pcm_velocity_reference_depths_m":[500,600],"velocity_references_are_width_layer":false,"abstract_core_depth_context_m":[150,200],"core_depth_context_is_fixed_width_layer":false,"velocity_errors_are_width_uncertainty":false,"float_sampling_band_is_width":false,"newer_35w_section_is_measurement_support":false,"net_flow_boundaries_resolved":false,"per_cruise_width_values_available":false,"campaign_years":[1978,1979,1980],"display_aria_label":"Atlantic SEUC: about 120 km 20 cm/s core width in the 1978–1980 study. Abstract about 100 km remains separate unresolved context, not a range or uncertainty. No fixed depth or annual width inferred.","display_caption":"About 120 km · source-defined 20 cm/s core. The abstract separately says about 100 km; no combined 100–120 km range or 110 km midpoint.","display_method_note":"1978–1980 regional summary; no width per cruise, fixed depth, numerical width error or net-flow boundary. 1000 db captions and 1000 m prose retained as distinct reference expressions.","comparison_figure":"figures/atlantic-seuc-molinari-1981-core-width.svg","audit_file":"research/atlantic-seuc-molinari-1981-core-width-scope-audit.json","audit_sha256":"577cccac98a3970272e7e2ab7a11bceba86138fec881adad570ba18d58c8ca1c"}},{"id":"northern-mediterranean-winter-width","current_id":"northern-mediterranean","name":"Northern Current","status":"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical","measurement_type":"published_regional_seasonal_summary","width_metric":"author_reported_current_width","approximate_width_km":25,"width_range_km":null,"range_interpretation":"No numerical uncertainty interval supplied for this approximate seasonal value.","geographic_scope":"Southern French coast / Gulf of Lion regional literature context; not a uniform width along the full Ligurian-Catalan route.","section_geometry":null,"section_orientation":"Not fixed in this regional synthesis.","layer":"Current envelope described with approximate seasonal vertical extent 450 m; width is not a measurement at every depth or a fixed-depth slice.","time_convention":"winter seasonal description in source introduction; not th