ribed California Undercurrent below 200 m.","time_convention":"October-March regional seasonal description in a February 1978 report; strongest flow described in January. Not a dated width survey, current-year observation or modern monthly climatology.","boundary_rule":"Author-reported approximate width; paired boundary coordinates, velocity threshold and sampling method are not specified.","source_url":"https://waves-vagues.dfo-mpo.gc.ca/library-bibliotheque/40591190_v2.pdf","source_citation":"Fisheries and Environment Canada, Working Group on West Coast Deepwater Oil Ports (1978), Potential Pacific Coast Oil Ports: A Comparative Environmental Risk Analysis, Volume II - Supplementary Appendices, February 1978.","source_locator":"Appendix II, section II.1, printed II-1 to II-2 (PDF pages 12-13), paragraph beginning The Davidson current; width and months on PDF page 13.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-03","source_publication_year":1978,"source_document_sha256":"ea4f05cbba6f7b955ba26a93359e237dc041f6d3c2dcbb4cc6ea11ce455dd6c6","source_evidence_kind":"published_historical_regional_synthesis","historical_summary":true,"extraction_method":"Approximate 64 km and October-March interval transcribed from full PDF prose. No figure digitized, route buffered or station distance interpreted as width.","whole_current_representative":false,"width_rank_eligible":false,"remaining_gates":["Review underlying observations, width boundaries and historical applicability.","Obtain regional repeated seasonal observations before annual variability or modern representative width.","Canonical measurement admission and release review."],"phase_label":"October-March (1978 regional summary)","phase_kind":"seasonal_summary","observed_period":null,"calendar_months":[10,11,12,1,2,3],"calendar_source_locator":"Appendix II section II.1, printed II-2 / PDF page 13: October to March along California and Oregon coasts.","source_quality_note":"Historical regional summary from 1978, not a present-day width measurement. Vancouver Island penetration is conditional; 25 and 50 km off Tofino are observation locations, not width boundaries. The separately described 50 km California Undercurrent is a different layer and current."},{"id":"gaspe-regional-typical-width-range","current_id":"gaspe","name":"Gaspé Current","status":"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical","measurement_type":"published_regional_summary","width_metric":"author_reported_current_width","approximate_width_km":null,"width_range_km":[10,20],"range_kind":"reported_typical_regional_width_span","is_confidence_interval":false,"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"range_interpretation":"Source-reported typical regional width span; no single midpoint or representative width selected. Not a confidence interval, matched seasonal pair or annual extrema.","geographic_scope":"Gaspe Peninsula coastal jet described in thesis introductory regional synthesis; not a measured uniform width along the estuary-to-Magdalen reference corridor.","section_geometry":null,"section_orientation":"Not specified for this typical regional prose range.","layer":"Upper coastal jet, described in the first approximately 40 m; range not assigned to every depth.","time_convention":"Regional typical-width summary in February 2022 thesis introduction; the adjacent summer maximum-speed clause does not make this a measured summer width range. No matched winter/summer widths or dated survey interval assigned.","boundary_rule":"Author-reported typical width; no paired boundary coordinates or reproducible velocity threshold supplied for the range.","source_url":"https://semaphore.uqar.ca/2055/1/Theau_Leclercq_fevrier2022.pdf","source_citation":"Leclercq, Théau (2022), Observations des remontées et des plongées des eaux en bordure du courant de Gaspé, master's thesis in oceanography, UQAR-ISMER, February 2022.","source_locator":"Printed page 5 / PDF page 21, paragraph on typical width 10-20 km; printed page 14 / PDF page 30, English introduction, width can reach 20 km.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-03","source_publication_year":2022,"source_document_sha256":"b8244831f7e593b0f5da2861f44658ccc8e9c4822cb9fe3b122e2e1e5654ae25","source_evidence_kind":"published_regional_literature_summary","extraction_method":"Typical 10-20 km range transcribed from full thesis prose, with corroborating English upper-width statement. No figure digitized, midpoint manufactured or route buffered.","whole_current_representative":false,"width_rank_eligible":false,"remaining_gates":["Review original observational definitions and temporal/along-route support behind the synthesis.","Obtain paired boundaries and compatible repeat sections before seasonal widths, annual ranges or representative width.","Canonical measurement admission and release review."],"phase_label":"Regional typical width (2022 synthesis)","phase_kind":"regional_summary","observed_period":null,"calendar_months":null,"source_quality_note":"Literature summary in an observational thesis, not a new dated width measurement from its transects. Exact boundaries and uncertainty remain unspecified."},{"id":"north-cape-northern-2007-profile-scale","current_id":"north-cape","name":"North Cape Current — Northern branch","status":"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical","measurement_type":"published_survey_profile_fit_scale","width_metric":"gaussian_e_folding_distance_from_profile_center","approximate_width_km":8,"width_range_km":null,"range_interpretation":"Approximate fitted effective scale; no fit confidence interval or annual variability range supplied.","geographic_scope":"Northern branch near the western Hopen Deep / Spitsbergen Bank polar frontal zone, Barents Sea. Not the Central branch or whole North Cape system.","section_geometry":null,"section_orientation":"Distance from frontal-section center across individual crossings; northward geographic velocity component fitted. Exact paired geographic boundaries unresolved.","layer":"Composite vertical support unresolved. Fig. 9 specifies a 20–80 m average for LS05; Fig. 10 does not explicitly establish that same fixed layer for all 15 crossings. Instrument generally sampled from about 20 m to 150 m or 15 m above bottom.","fixed_layer_bounds_m":null,"time_convention":"15 frontal crossings during summer expeditions in 2007. Paper describes a 29 May–10 June 2007 cruise, but exact composite sampling bounds are unresolved; not a recurring seasonal width.","boundary_rule":"Source approximates the mean northward velocity profile by V(x)=17 exp(-(x/8)^2), x in km and V in cm/s, and calls 8 km mean effective width. OSW infers center-to-e-folding scale from the equation; no paired-edge full span is admitted.","boundary_sides":"fitted_center_to_e_folding_distance","full_width_inference_eligible":false,"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"seasonal_playback_eligible":false,"is_confidence_interval":false,"source_url":"https://physical-oceanography.ru/repository/issues/2017/02/05/20170205.pdf","source_citation":"Morozov, Pavlov, Pavlova and Fedorov (2017), Polar Frontal Zone of the Barents Sea Western Trough Based on the Direct Measurements in 2007, Physical Oceanography 2, 36–50, doi:10.22449/1573-160X-2017-2-36-50.","source_locator":"Abstract; Introduction pp. 36–37; Instruments p. 37; Stationary currents p. 38; Currents pp. 45–47, Fig. 9 and Fig. 10, especially Gaussian-fit paragraph on p. 47.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-03","source_evidence_kind":"published_front_centered_velocity_profile_fit","extraction_method":"Transcribed source fit scale and 15-crossing count; metric interpretation inferred algebraically from stated Gaussian equation. No figure digitized or converted full width added.","whole_current_representative":false,"width_rank_eligible":false,"phase_kind":"survey_profile_composite","phase_label":"2007 frontal-crossing composite","observed_period":null,"calendar_months":null,"cruise_context_period":{"start":"2007-05-29","end":"2007-06-10"},"cruise_context_is_composite_sampling_