ection","is_confidence_interval":false,"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"range_interpretation":"Approximate author-reported span for the upwelling-season mean undercurrent section. Not annual extrema, confidence limits or a mean of instantaneous widths; no midpoint selected.","geographic_scope":"Reference section at 18 N, pooling coastal measurements from 17–19 N by local bathymetry. Not a uniform whole-coast width.","section_geometry":null,"section_orientation":"Across-shore reference section; rotated alongshore velocity and topographic remapping, not extracted paired edge coordinates.","layer":"Poleward subsurface flow with core context about 100–200 m in the seasonal mean. No fixed-depth boundary pair assigned; equatorward shelf surface flow and deeper return remain separate.","time_convention":"December–April upwelling-season convention; five cruises sampled in January–April during 2005–2011 within the study-wide 2005–2016 campaign set. December label is not evidence for sampled December geometry.","boundary_rule":"Author reports 30–40 km in Conclusion; numerical velocity threshold and paired boundaries for this prose width were not extracted.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2018JC014264","source_citation":"Klenz, Dengler and Brandt (2018), Seasonal Variability of the Mauritania Current and Hydrography at 18 N, JGR: Oceans 123, 8122–8137, doi:10.1029/2018JC014264.","source_locator":"Section 5 width statement; section 2.1 and Table 2 sampling/remapping; section 3.1 and Figure 5 seasonal mean context.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-03","source_publication_year":2018,"source_evidence_kind":"published_observational_seasonal_mean_summary","extraction_method":"Width span transcribed from publisher conclusion; figures, edges and source arrays not digitized.","whole_current_representative":false,"width_rank_eligible":false,"remaining_gates":["Recover paired boundaries and thresholds for the source seasonal mean.","Obtain compatible relaxation/other-season repeat widths; no annual extrema yet.","Independent canonical measurement admission and release review."],"phase_label":"December–April poleward undercurrent · seasonal mean","phase_kind":"seasonal_mean_width_range","observed_period":null,"calendar_months":[12,1,2,3,4],"source_quality_note":"Five upwelling cruises support this mean. August 2016 was excluded from both seasonal means. The 60 km transport window and 200 km surface-flow context are not current widths.","calendar_source_locator":"Section 2.1 seasonal cruise assignment and Figure 5 caption.","seasonal_playback_eligible":false,"seasonal_mean_context":{"reference_latitude_degrees":18,"pooled_latitude_bounds_degrees":[17,19],"sample_years":[2005,2011],"study_years":[2005,2016],"cruise_ids":["P320","P347","P348","ATA3","MSM17/4"],"sampled_months":[1,2,3,4],"averaging_rule":"Measurements rotated locally, sorted by water depth, remapped onto reference topography, then assigned to source seasonal means.","width_of_mean_section":true,"mean_of_instantaneous_widths":false,"paired_edges_extracted":false,"fixed_depth_bounds_m":null}},{"id":"atlantic-secc-1994-03-described-band-span","current_id":"atlantic-south-equatorial-countercurrent","name":"Atlantic South Equatorial Countercurrent","status":"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical","measurement_type":"published_month_section_angular_span","width_metric":"author_reported_meridional_angular_span","approximate_width_km":220,"width_range_km":null,"range_interpretation":"Converted local band span only. No uncertainty interval, uniform along-route width, annual range or continuous current axis inferred.","geographic_scope":"March 1994 CITHER 2 section at 30 W, reported current band 6–8 S; local meridional span, not whole-current extent.","section_geometry":null,"section_orientation":"Reported meridional section span; no exact flow-normal reinterpretation or observed paired-edge geometry.","layer":"Two eastward-core contexts near 40 m and 