ian Current","status":"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical","measurement_type":"published_regional_scalar_width_summary","width_metric":"author_reported_regional_current_scale","width_metric_label":"typical current; institutional regional prose summary","approximate_width_km":30,"width_range_km":null,"range_interpretation":"No annual extrema or numerical uncertainty interval supplied.","geographic_scope":"Southern Coral Sea and northern New South Wales boundary-current description; no specific width section or endpoints supplied.","section_geometry":null,"section_orientation":"Unspecified in institutional prose; no occupied section extracted.","layer":"Source describes a typical 200 m depth extent; this does not specify a fixed depth or vertically averaged layer for the 30 km width.","time_convention":"Undated typical description in a plan dated 25 September 2014 for 2015-25. These are document dates, not width observation dates or a seasonal cycle.","boundary_rule":"Typical current-width description without paired edges, a speed threshold or a specified occupied section.","source_url":"https://imos.org.au/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/NSW-IMOS_Node_Plan_2015-25_Final.pdf","source_citation":"Robertson, Ingleton, Doblin, Suthers and Roughan, NSW-IMOS Node Science and Implementation Plan 2015-25, edited Robin Robertson, dated 25 September 2014, section 3.3.1.","source_locator":"Section 3.3.1, printed page 23 (PDF page index 22), first paragraph; plan date on printed page 2: 25 September 2014.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-04","source_evidence_kind":"institutional_science_plan_prose_synthesis","extraction_method":"Approximate scalar transcribed from institutional PDF text; no figure, influence envelope, array span or route buffer measured.","whole_current_representative":false,"width_rank_eligible":false,"full_width_inference_eligible":false,"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"seasonal_playback_eligible":false,"is_confidence_interval":false,"phase_label":"Typical current width in NSW-IMOS plan","phase_kind":"regional_scalar_summary","observed_period":null,"calendar_months":null,"fixed_layer_bounds_m":null,"regional_scalar_context":{"audit_file":"research/east-australian-imos-regional-width-scope-audit.json","audit_sha256":"c051be2ee7863179fc447a22a9055f7ff501ed8dcc0ed5f104f390d3343e4b40","boundary_coordinates_supplied":false,"bathymetry_is_measurement_layer":false,"reported_depth_extent_is_fixed_measurement_layer":false},"remaining_gates":["Inspect Mata et al. (2000) and Ridgway and Dunn (2003) for the width convention and support.","Recover compatible layer-specific cross-flow sections and observations through seasons.","Independent scientific claim admission."],"source_quality_note":"Underlying width convention remains unverified. CSIRO describes a separate 100 km strong-influence width, which is not combined with the 30 km typical current summary into a seasonal range. The 240 km mooring array and 200 km eddy diameters are different quantities. Institutional PDF text was inspected; screenshot acquisition failed."},{"id":"leeuwin-a101-monthly-fit-04","current_id":"leeuwin","name":"Leeuwin Current","status":"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical","measurement_type":"published_monthly_mean_fitted_width","width_metric":"source_fitted_cross_flow_width","width_metric_label":"a101; mean of source fitted widths","approximate_width_km":132,"width_range_km":null,"range_interpretation":"Two extracted monthly climatological values do not establish a full annual range or a confidence interval.","geographic_scope":"TOPEX/Poseidon ascending track a101 crossing near 26 S, west of Western Australia. No monthly lateral-edge coordinates extracted.","section_geometry":null,"section_orientation":"Source cross-flow width corrected from oblique satellite track using theta=43.45 degrees.","layer":"Surface geostrophic diagnostic from absolute SSH minus AUSGeoid98. The 80 m layer is a transport assumption, not the width measurement layer.","time_convention":"Calendar-month composite of per-cycle fitted widths. Section 3.3 says January 1993-July 2002; Fig. 7 caption says through August 2002. Exact combined period unresolved; no single-year occupation inferred.","boundary_rule":"Source w=1.89*L*cos(theta), described as about 50% of maximum fitted velocity; preserve approximate source coefficient rather than exact half-maximum conversion.","source_url":"https://pdfs.semanticscholar.org/21be/8b2802335b0f945b23cde6ece4d5e3647f09.pdf","source_citation":"Deng, Hwang, Coleman and Featherstone (2008), Seasonal and Interannual Variations of the Leeuwin Current off Western Australia from TOPEX/Poseidon Satellite Altimetry, TAO 19, 135-149, doi:10.3319/TAO.2008.19.1-2.135(SA).","source_locator":"Section 3.3, printed page 143, paragraph discussing current width at a101; Fig. 7d on page 144; section 2.2 equations 1-3 on page 138 and angle convention on page 139.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-04","source_evidence_kind":"published_altimetry_fitted_monthly_width","extraction_method":"Approximate April/September values transcribed from source prose and visually checked against Fig. 7d; no other monthly points inferred.","whole_current_representative":false,"width_rank_eligible":false,"full_width_inference_eligible":false,"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"seasonal_playback_eligible":false,"is_confidence_interval":false,"phase_label":"April climatological fitted width","phase_kind":"monthly_climatological_fit","observed_period":null,"calendar_months":[4],"fixed_layer_bounds_m":null,"remaining_gates":["Extract all 12 months with plot calibration and extraction margins before annual display.","Reconcile July/August period labels, fitting model and approximate half-maximum convention.","Review near-coastal gaps, Gaussian filtering and current-angle assumptions.","Independent scientific claim admission."],"source_quality_note":"50 km filter window is not current width. Table 1 gives 105 km mean with 35 km RMS variability, not