fic admission and protected-main publication."]},{"id":"alaska-coastal-gulf-jarosz-2017-typical-width","current_id":"alaska-coastal-gulf","name":"Alaska Coastal Current (Gulf of Alaska)","status":"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical","measurement_type":"published_regional_scalar_width_summary","width_metric":"author_reported_regional_current_scale","width_metric_label":"typical Gulf-of-Alaska coastal flow; regional prose synthesis","approximate_width_km":35,"width_range_km":null,"range_interpretation":"No annual extrema or numerical uncertainty interval supplied.","geographic_scope":"Gulf-of-Alaska coastal shelf current; no width transferred to offshore Alaska Current, Alaskan Stream or the Arctic/Bering namesake.","section_geometry":null,"section_orientation":"Unspecified in regional prose; no occupied section extracted.","layer":"Regional coastal-current description; no fixed measurement layer assigned to the typical-width statement.","time_convention":"Introductory regional literature summary in a 2017 winter study. The October 2012-March 2013 experiment dates do not date this typical width; seasonal variation is qualitative only.","boundary_rule":"Author-reported typical regional width; no paired boundaries, velocity threshold or width occupation interval assigned to the 35 km introduction statement.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/2016JC012102","source_citation":"Jarosz, Wang, Wijesekera, Pegau and Moum (2017), Flow variability within the Alaska Coastal Current in winter, JGR Oceans 122, 3884-3906, doi:10.1002/2016JC012102.","source_locator":"Section 1 Introduction, second paragraph: typical approximately 35 km width; distinct shelf circulation from subarctic gyre in preceding paragraph.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-08","source_evidence_kind":"published_regional_prose_synthesis","extraction_method":"Approximate 35 km scalar transcribed from publisher Introduction; no axis, footprint or paired edges reconstructed.","whole_current_representative":false,"width_rank_eligible":false,"full_width_inference_eligible":false,"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"seasonal_playback_eligible":false,"is_confidence_interval":false,"phase_label":"Typical Gulf-of-Alaska coastal width (regional summary)","phase_kind":"regional_scalar_summary","observed_period":null,"calendar_months":null,"fixed_layer_bounds_m":null,"regional_scalar_context":{"audit_file":"research/alaska-coastal-gulf-jarosz-2017-regional-width-scope-audit.json","audit_sha256":"308e05e7c1c8122aaee0b917b85822b1162b8b25021aa0f77387eca11714843b","boundary_coordinates_supplied":false,"bathymetry_is_measurement_layer":false},"remaining_gates":["Review original width definitions behind the introductory literature synthesis.","Obtain paired boundaries and compatible repeated sections before seasonal dimension ranges.","Independent scientific and canonical admission review."],"source_quality_note":"Typical-width literature statement, not a measured winter width from the article experiment. Original contributing definitions remain unreviewed."},{"id":"mindanao-schonau-2015-mean-surface-offshore-extent","current_id":"mindanao-current","name":"Mindanao Current","status":"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical","measurement_type":"published_mean_surface_offshore_extent_range","width_metric":"author_reported_mean_surface_equatorward_offshore_extent","approximate_width_km":null,"width_range_km":[250,300],"range_kind":"author_reported_approximate_offshore_extent_of_mean_surface_flow","range_interpretation":"Approximate range in the author’s prose description of one averaged surface section; not uncertainty, seasonal extrema or a paired-boundary full width.","geographic_scope":"Oblique mean line from 8.16 N, 126.61 E to 8.77 N, 130 E off Mindanao. Profiles within 80 km were projected and objectively mapped; not an along-current envelope.","section_geometry":null,"section_orientation":"Oblique mean line; reported offshore distance retained without converting it to paired cross-flow edges.","layer":"Surface expression of averaged absolute geostrophic equatorward flow. The 0–1000 m glider velocity reference is not a fixed measurement layer for this extent.","fixed_layer_bounds_m":null,"time_convention":"Spatial and temporal mean of glider profiles; campaign context June 2009–July 2014. Exact contributing dates of the Figure 2 mean unresolved.","boundary_rule":"Author-reported offshore extent of equatorward mean flow, not a diagnosed pair of current boundaries. Figure 2 contours are 0.1 m/s intervals; no numerical extent threshold assigned.","source_url":"https://www.soest.hawaii.edu/oceanography/bo/Schonau_etal_TOS2015.pdf","source_citation":"Schönau et al. (2015), The Mindanao Current: Mean Structure and Connectivity, Oceanography 28(4), 34–45, doi:10.5670/oceanog.2015.79.","source_locator":"Printed p.38 / PDF p.6, Velocity and Transport, glider paragraph and Figure 2a; mean-line sampling described on pp.36–37 / PDF pp.4–5.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-08","source_evidence_kind":"published_observational_mean_section_description","extraction_method":"250–300 km transcribed from p.38 prose after inspecting Figure 2a; no edge digitization, midpoint or route buffer.","whole_current_representative":false,"width_rank_eligible":false,"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"seasonal_playback_eligible":false,"full_width_inference_eligible":false,"is_confidence_interval":false,"calendar_months":null,"observed_period":null,"boundary_sides":"author_reported_one_sided_offshore_extent","phase_label":"glider mean surface offshore extent","phase_kind":"mean_offshore_extent_range","remaining_gates":["Obtain contributing profile dates and machine-readable velocity fields.","Diagnose paired edges with a consistent threshold before full-width or seasonal ranges.","Independent scientific and canonical admission review."],"mean_offshore_context":{"mean_line_endpoints_lon_lat":[[126.61,8.16],[130,8.77]],"projection_corridor_km":