null,"range_kind":"approximate_regional_point_no_reported_interval","range_interpretation":"One approximate regional background value; no numerical uncertainty, range, confidence interval, annual extrema or seasonal observations supplied.","geographic_scope":"Eastern Gulf of Alaska boundary flow along the continental slope, distinct from the Alaskan Stream in the northwestern gulf and inner-shelf Alaska Coastal Current. No paired width edges or exact terminal gates supplied.","section_geometry":null,"section_orientation":"No reproducible transverse section endpoints supplied for the regional breadth description.","layer":"Regional current flow; fixed numerical width layer unspecified. Weak horizontal and vertical shears do not establish a depth interval.","time_convention":"Regional background synthesis in a 2002 article; no dated width occupation or width climatology. Year-round persistence and GLOBEC program dates are separate context.","boundary_rule":"Author-reported approximate regional breadth. No paired edge positions or velocity cutoff extracted. Sentence continues on p50 to contrast the Alaskan Stream and cite Reed and Schumacher (1986).","source_url":"https://tos.org/oceanography/article/the-northeast-pacific-globec-program-coastal-gulf-of-alaska","source_citation":"Weingartner et al. (2002), The Northeast Pacific GLOBEC Program: Coastal Gulf of Alaska, Oceanography 15(2), 48-63, doi:10.5670/oceanog.2002.21.","source_locator":"Physical Setting, printed p49 (PDF page 2), right column final paragraph; sentence continuation on p50 (PDF page 3), left column below Figure 1.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-08","source_evidence_kind":"published_original_regional_background_synthesis","extraction_method":"Approximate point transcribed from visually inspected publisher original prose; no current axis or map width digitization.","whole_current_representative":false,"width_rank_eligible":false,"full_width_inference_eligible":false,"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"seasonal_playback_eligible":false,"is_confidence_interval":false,"phase_label":"Regional eastern Gulf background synthesis","phase_kind":"regional_summary","observed_period":null,"calendar_months":null,"fixed_layer_bounds_m":null,"uncertainty_km":null,"source_quality_note":"Original publisher PDF and p49/p50 visually inspected. Approximate regional description, not a new GLOBEC width calculation. Underlying cited boundary method and attribution remain unreviewed.","remaining_gates":["Resolve the cited original width support and paired boundary method.","Obtain compatible repeat sections before monthly or annual variation.","Independent scientific admission."],"original_regional_context":{"width_passage_visually_inspected":true,"underlying_width_source":"Reed and Schumacher (1986) at the end of the sentence on p50; application to the Alaska breadth is not independently resolved.","underlying_width_methods_reviewed":false,"survey_years_are_width_occupations":false,"drifter_depth_is_width_layer":false,"forcing_climatologies_are_width_climatology":false,"year_round_persistence_is_monthly_width_series":false,"alaskan_stream_width_is_range_endpoint":false,"coastal_confinement_is_alaska_width":false,"shelf_breadth_is_current_width":false,"boundary_coordinates_extracted":false,"protocol_file":"plans/alaska-regional-width-protocol-v1.md","protocol_sha256":"21c30fc5f5de4b01ca8ff53e2ac382b2e55052a38618a935669b3729b460b553","display_caption":"Eastern Gulf of Alaska boundary current · one approximate 300 km regional background description. Numerical uncertainty, width range, fixed layer and observation dates unknown. GLOBEC survey dates, drifter depth and forcing climatologies do not define this width. No annual range, monthly samples or mapped edges inferred.","display_method_note":"Publisher p49 and its p50 sentence continuation inspected. The narrower Alaskan Stream and inner-shelf Alaska Coastal Current are separate features. The cited original boundary method remains unreviewed.","audit_file":"research/alaska-weingartner-2002-regional-width-scope-audit.json","audit_sha256":"475b2cbc7c21e6aac907e2a61153b50088fb77010053f0957e6f2cf44f5535ad"}},{"id":"pacific-euc-wang-2022-background-width","current_id":"pacific-equatorial-undercurrent","name":"Pacific Equatorial Undercurrent","status":"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical","measurement_type":"published_regional_summary","width_metric":"author_reported_current_width","approximate_width_km":400,"width_range_km":null,"range_kind":"approximate_regional_point_no_reported_interval","range_interpretation":"One approximate regional background value; no numerical uncertainty, range, confidence interval, annual extrema or seasonal observations supplied.","geographic_scope":"Pacific eastward equatorial subsurface jet; background approximation without a fixed section longitude or paired edge coordinates. Not the generic cross-basin family or Atlantic/Indian EUC.","section_geometry":null,"section_orientation":"No reproducible transverse section endpoints supplied for the regional breadth description.","layer":"Subsurface current background; adjacent approximate thickness and 50–200 m core depths are context, not a fixed width measurement layer.","time_convention":"Background synthesis in a 2022 article; no dated width occupation or monthly width climatology. Simulation years and transport/velocity climatologies have different support.","boundary_rule":"Author-reported approximate background width. No velocity cutoff, paired boundaries or explicit transverse section extracted. Model transport boxes are not width boundaries.","source_url":"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2022.908939/full","source_citation":"Wang et al. (2022), Wind-Driven Mechanisms for the Variations of the Pacific Equatorial Undercurrent Based on Adjoint Sensitivity Analysis, Frontiers in Marine Science 9:908939, doi:10.3389/fmars.2022.908939.","source_locator":"Introduction opening paragraph, printed p1 (PDF page 1); different model/transport supports in sections 2.1–2.2 and Figures 1/2, printed pp3–4.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-08","source_evidence_kind":"published_original_regional_background_synthesis","extraction_method":"Approximate width transcribed from visually inspected publisher original p1 prose; no map, current axis or model transport-box width digitization.","whole_current_representative":false,"width_rank_eligible":false,"full_width_inference_eligible":false,"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"seasonal_playback_eligible":false,"is_confidence_interval":false,"phase_label":"Pacific subsurface jet background synthesis","phase_kind":"regional_summary","observed_period":null,"calendar_months":null,"fixed_layer_bounds_m":null,"uncertainty_km":null,"source_quality_note":"Original publisher p1 width and p4 transport/velocity context visually inspected. Background 400 km is not a derived width from the adjoint experiment. Underlying historical width method and exact attribution remain unreviewed.","remaining_gates":["Resolve the original historical width support and paired boundary method.","Obtain compatible repeated width sections before monthly or annual variation.","Independent scientific admission."],"original_regional_context":{"width_passage_visually_inspected":true,"underlying_width_source":"Cromwell et al. (1954) cited in the opening current description; exact support for the background width and original measurement method not independently resolved.","underlying_width_methods_reviewed":false,"approximate_thickness_is_fixed_width_layer":false,"core_depths_are_fixed_width_layer":false,"model_transport_bounds_are_width_edges":false,"model_transport_depths_are_width_layer":false,"model_years_are_width_occupations":false,"transport_velocity_climatology_is_width_climatology":false,"transport_seasonality_is_width_seasonality":false,"other_publication_width_is_range_endpoint":false,"cross_basin_width_inheritance_eligible":false,"boundary_coordinates_extracted":false,"transport_context":{"longitude_deg_e":165,"latitude_bounds_deg":[-3,3],"gecco_depth_bounds_m":[87.5,310],"hycom_depth_bounds_m":[85,310],"velocity_average_depth_bounds_m":[100,300],"hycom_tao_velocity_climatology_years":[1994,2013],"source_locator":"Sections 2.1–2.2, equation 6 and Figures 1/2, printed pp3–4","is_width_measurement_support":false},"protocol_file":"plans/pacific-euc-background-width-protocol-v1.md","protocol_sha256":"ef339570824337ee7a398ffd18a4aaba5e151c177912ce74da958222b09eec1b","display_caption":"Pacific eastward subsurface jet · one approximate 400 km background width. Numerical uncertainty, width range, fixed measurement layer and observation dates unknown. Transport and velocity seasonal cycles do not supply monthly widths. No annual range or mapped edges inferred.","display_method_note":"Publisher p1 width prose and p4 transport context inspected. About 200 m thickness and 50–200 m core depths are separate descriptions. The 3°S–3°N transport box is not a width observation. Historical boundary method remains unreviewed; no transfer to other basin currents.","audit_file":"research/pacific-euc-wang-2022-background-width-scope-audit.json","audit_sha256":"9be49243e762e82c9a7ce0e0348a3a8e29c4c8973b34f4773a4ebdb49799c998"}},{"id":"atlantic-euc-gouriou-1988-background-width","current_id":"atlantic-equatorial-undercurrent","name":"Atlantic Equatorial Undercurrent","status":"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical","measurement_type":"published_regional_summary","width_metric":"author_reported_current_width","approximate_width_km":200,"width_range_km":null,"range_kind":"approximate_regional_point_no_reported_interval","range_interpretation":"One approximate regional background value; no numerical uncertainty, range, confidence interval, annual extrema or seasonal observations supplied.","geographic_scope":"Atlantic eastward subsurface equatorial jet, called Lomonosov current; Brazil to Gulf of Guinea background description without paired boundary coordinates or a specified transverse section.","section_geometry":null,"section_orientation":"No reproducible transverse section endpoints supplied for the regional breadth description.","layer":"Subsurface current background. Adjacent 150 m thickness and 50–125 m core depths do not define a fixed width measurement layer.","time_convention":"1988 French synthesis; no dated width occupation. Compilation years, dated example sections and transport occupations are separate supports.","boundary_rule":"Approximate author-reported background width; no paired edges or boundary threshold directly resolved. Transport cutoff is not adopted as this width method.","source_url":"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/divers11-10/34183.pdf","source_citation":"Y. Gouriou (1988), chapter III, section 3.3.2, printed p16, in Fonteneau and Marcille (eds.), FAO Fisheries Technical Paper 292 (French edition), ISBN 92-5-202652-5.","source_locator":"Printed p16 / PDF page 31, section 3.3.2; title/copyright PDF pages 2–3; Figure 3.4 printed p18 / PDF page 33.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-08","source_evidence_kind":"published_original_regional_background_synthesis","extraction_method":"Approximate breadth transcribed from visually inspected institutional original; no contour, transport or coordinate digitization.","whole_current_representative":false,"width_rank_eligible":false,"full_width_inference_eligible":false,"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"seasonal_playback_eligible":false,"is_confidence_interval":false,"phase_label":"Atlantic subsurface jet background synthesis","phase_kind":"regional_summary","observed_period":null,"calendar_months":null,"fixed_layer_bounds_m":null,"uncertainty_km":null,"source_quality_note":"Original French volume confirms 200 km prose. Exact historical paired-boundary support remains unresolved. The later English OCR version and dated Voituriez sections are not independent 200 km width observations.","remaining_gates":["Resolve historical background-width boundary method and exact attribution.","Extract compatible repeated transverse sections before seasonal dimensions.","Independent scientific admission."],"original_regional_context":{"width_passage_visually_inspected":true,"underlying_width_source":"Voituriez (1983) cited near the description; its source sections were reviewed separately, without directly establishing this regional 200 km boundary method.","underlying_width_methods_reviewed":false,"thickness_is_fixed_width_layer":false,"core_depths_are_fixed_width_layer":false,"core_position_oscillation_is_width_range":false,"compilation_years_are_width_occupations":false,"figure_section_dates_are_background_width_dates":false,"garp_transport_dates_are_width_occupations":false,"transport_cutoff_is_background_width_boundary":false,"translation_is_independent_width_observation":false,"cross_basin_width_inheritance_eligible":false,"boundary_coordinates_extracted":false,"protocol_file":"plans/atlantic-euc-background-width-protocol-v1.md","protocol_sha256":"f37545d040de00e884348a6aee729c18db00f40cc7db65beb903003459298279","display_caption":"Atlantic eastward subsurface jet · one approximate 200 km background width. Fixed width layer, numerical uncertainty, paired edges and observation dates unknown. No annual range or seasonal width series inferred.","display_method_note":"Original French FAO p16 inspected. 150 m thickness, 50–125 m core depths and core-position oscillations are separate descriptions. The 1988 synthesis and 1993 English version are not two width samples; dated sections and transport thresholds do not date or define this background breadth.","audit_file":"research/atlantic-euc-gouriou-1988-background-width-scope-audit.json","audit_sha256":"f6881f5090e36b3ae3b82459b52d9b5fd06fb93a23cd25ffc3202beb94a80433"}},{"id":"kuroshio-extension-sasaki-2013-monthly-field-width","current_id":"kuroshio-extension","name":"Kuroshio Extension","status":"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical","measurement_type":"published_regional_summary","width_metric":"author_reported_current_width","approximate_width_km":100,"width_range_km":null,"range_kind":"approximate_regional_point_no_reported_interval","range_interpretation":"One approximate regional background value; no numerical uncertainty, range, confidence interval, annual extrema or seasonal observations supplied.","geographic_scope":"Intense Kuroshio Extension jet in monthly mean fields, extending eastward from Japan to the date line; no transverse boundary coordinates extracted.","section_geometry":null,"section_orientation":"Author-reported meridional width; not assumed normal to the meandering jet.","layer":"Surface SSH and geostrophic velocity context; no fixed vertical width layer supplied.","time_convention":"Monthly mean fields summarized in source prose; no dated width series extracted. January 2005 is the illustrative Figure 1b field.","boundary_rule":"Author-reported meridional jet width. Continuous SSH contours and peak velocity locate the axis; no paired width edges or threshold resolved.","source_url":"https://eprints.lib.hokudai.ac.jp/repo/huscap/all/52934/jpo-d-12-096.1.pdf","source_citation":"Sasaki, Y. N., S. Minobe and N. Schneider (2013), Decadal Response of the Kuroshio Extension Jet to Rossby Waves: Observation and Thin-Jet Theory, JPO 43(2):442–456, doi:10.1175/JPO-D-12-096.1.","source_locator":"Printed p445 / PDF page 5, section 3 first paragraph; data/methods pp443–444; Figure 1 printed p444 / PDF page 4.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-08","source_evidence_kind":"published_original_regional_monthly_field_summary","extraction_method":"Approximate width transcribed from visually inspected original; no contour, coordinate or velocity-profile digitization.","whole_current_representative":false,"width_rank_eligible":false,"full_width_inference_eligible":false,"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"seasonal_playback_eligible":false,"is_confidence_interval":false,"phase_label":"Meridional jet width in monthly mean fields","phase_kind":"regional_summary","observed_period":null,"calendar_months":null,"fixed_layer_bounds_m":null,"uncertainty_km":null,"source_quality_note":"Monthly mean is a temporal operator, not a recovered month-by-month width series. The separate 200 km climatological meridional scale has different support; it is not an interval endpoint.","remaining_gates":["Resolve a reproducible meridional width boundary rule and exact transverse support.","Extract dated compatible sections before seasonal dimensions or playback.","Independent scientific admission."],"original_regional_context":{"width_passage_visually_inspected":true,"underlying_width_source":"Original section 3 and Figure 1; axis method inspected separately from unresolved paired width method.","underlying_width_methods_reviewed":false,"monthly_mean_is_dated_width_series":false,"illustrative_figure_date_is_width_occupation":false,"analysis_period_is_width_occupation":false,"climatological_scale_is_width_range_endpoint":false,"jet_displacement_is_width_variation":false,"axis_search_contours_are_width_edges":false,"eof_anomaly_scale_is_width_measurement":false,"low_pass_shading_is_monthly_width_series":false,"meridional_width_is_flow_normal_width":false,"boundary_coordinates_extracted":false,"temporal_operator":"monthly_mean","illustrative_figure_month":"2005-01","analysis_period_context":{"start":"1993-01","end":"2010-12","is_width_measurement_support":false},"data_context":{"product":"AVISO monthly absolute dynamic height and surface geostrophic velocities","grid":"1/3 degree Mercator","mean_dynamic_topography":"Rio and Hernandez (2004)","low_pass_context":"9-month running mean for low-frequency analyses; Figure 1a standard deviations explicitly filtered; Figure 1b monthly mean distinct."},"climatological_scale_context":{"meridional_scale_km":200,"temporal_operator":"climatological_mean","geographic_scope":"Japan coast near 35°N to 165°E","source_locator":"Printed p445, section 3 first paragraph / Figure 1a","is_width_sample":false,"is_range_endpoint":false,"uncertainty_km":null},"protocol_file":"plans/kuroshio-extension-width-averaging-protocol-v1.md","protocol_sha256":"bac962694f1a0f2e0560218ace30240e3f0f8716ef5e4a8edef53c0bd7f99d79","display_caption":"Monthly mean fields · approximate 100 km meridional jet width, extending to the date line. No dated width series, numerical uncertainty, paired edges or annual range extracted.","display_method_note":"Separate context: the climatological jet has a reported 200 km meridional scale from Japan to 165°E. Different temporal and geographic supports; no 100–200 km seasonal range. Farther downstream, shifts of the narrow jet broaden its long-term mean. January 2005 illustrates a monthly SSH field; 60–120 cm contours locate the axis search region, not width edges.","audit_file":"research/kuroshio-extension-sasaki-2013-width-averaging-scope-audit.json","audit_sha256":"dfa44d57f053ac0cd8af32abcfdb0c5dcbdc63a3937c64abf14c79a2cb9370c7"}},{"id":"ngcu-zenk-1999-vitiaz-width-constraint","current_id":"new-guinea-coastal-undercurrent","name":"New Guinea Coastal Undercurrent","status":"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical","measurement_type":"published_regional_summary","width_metric":"author_reported_current_width","approximate_width_km":null,"width_range_km":null,"range_kind":"author_reported_order_of_magnitude_less_than_scale","range_interpretation":"Source O(<20 km) preserves an approximate less-than size description; not a measured 20 km point, rigorous hard bound, 0–20 km interval, uncertainty or seasonal extrema.","geographic_scope":"Local bands near the western exit of Vitiaz Strait; downstream central Bismarck Sea widening retained as context, not a whole-current dimension.","section_geometry":null,"section_orientation":"Local Doppler band breadth; exact transverse orientation and paired coordinates unresolved.","layer":"Subsurface slope-parallel current described near 200 m. No fixed width layer or paired depth-specific edges extracted.","time_convention":"SONNE cruise 113 context (10 October–19 November 1996); exact Doppler width occupations unresolved. March 1999 is publication, not observation.","boundary_rule":"Author-reported order-of-magnitude less-than band size. Exceeding 80 cm/s describes speed, not an adopted width-edge cutoff.","source_url":"https://oceanrep.geomar.de/1816/1/news34.pdf","source_citation":"Zenk, W., G. Siedler, J. Holfort and O. Boebel (1999), Float Observations Showing the Equatorial Crossing of Antarctic Intermediate Water in the Western Pacific, International WOCE Newsletter 34 (March), pp10–14, printed p13. Unpublished manuscript / work-in-progress newsletter report.","source_locator":"Printed/PDF p13 first column, continuation from p10; article pp10–14. Copyright PDF page 44. Figure 3 cruise-label conflict on p13.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-08","source_evidence_kind":"published_original_local_doppler_band_size_constraint","extraction_method":"Qualifier and reference size transcribed from visually inspected original; no profile digitization, exact crossing pairing or doubled downstream value.","whole_current_representative":false,"width_rank_eligible":false,"full_width_inference_eligible":false,"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"seasonal_playback_eligible":false,"is_confidence_interval":false,"phase_label":"Vitiaz exit Doppler band size constraint","phase_kind":"regional_summary","observed_period":null,"calendar_months":null,"fixed_layer_bounds_m":null,"uncertainty_km":null,"source_quality_note":"Work-in-progress newsletter report, not a peer-reviewed width series. Cruise 113 in prose conflicts with cruise 133 in Figure 3 caption. Salinity sections and float trajectories do not supply width boundaries.","remaining_gates":["Recover Doppler crossings, exact width layer and paired boundary rule.","Resolve cruise-label conflict and occupation support before dated widths.","Recover independently measured downstream dimensions; no factor-of-two arithmetic admission.","Independent scientific admission."],"original_regional_context":{"width_passage_visually_inspected":true,"underlying_width_source":"Zenk et al. (1999), p13; cited SONNE report inspected for ADCP context, not a resolved paired width definition.","underlying_width_methods_reviewed":false,"reference_scale_is_point_width":false,"notation_is_rigorous_upper_bound":false,"zero_to_reference_is_width_range":false,"downstream_doubling_is_numeric_width":false,"downstream_widening_is_seasonal_range":false,"speed_exceedance_is_width_cutoff":false,"core_depth_is_fixed_width_layer":false,"adcp_depth_coverage_is_fixed_width_layer":false,"salinity_section_is_width_boundary":false,"cruise_dates_are_width_occupations":false,"publication_month_is_width_observation":false,"float_dates_are_width_occupations":false,"boundary_coordinates_extracted":false,"cruise_context":{"prose_cruise_number":"113","figure_3_caption_cruise_number":"133","cruise_number_conflict":true,"voyage_start":"1996-10-10","voyage_end":"1996-11-19","is_width_measurement_support":false},"downstream_context":{"reported_core_widening_factor":2,"location":"central Bismarck Sea","derived_width_km":null,"is_seasonal_variation":false},"method_context":{"local_speed_exceeds_cm_s":80,"core_depth_context_m":200,"adcp_coverage_context_m":[350,400],"is_width_boundary_method":false},"supporting_report":{"source_url":"https://oceanrep.geomar.de/id/eprint/2244/1/IFM-BER_288.pdf","source_locator":"Printed p16 / PDF page 17, ADCP subsection; printed pp3 and 8–10 voyage context; no paired width extraction.","source_document_file":"research/source-data/siedler-sonne-1997/journal-article.pdf","source_document_bytes":4094903,"source_document_sha256":"cc9e293b98a47581b9d162c63781af1e5842d6aa0de403a7f06941ea7e6f4cca","acquisition_file":"research/source-data/siedler-sonne-1997/acquisition.json","acquisition_sha256":"31672631b098531dc6d707525055183e08b3b04e25c43381722bb6f694165