orted more-than scale for a broadly defined eastward flow band; not a 2000 km point, rigorous lower bound, finite interval, uncertainty or seasonal range.","geographic_scope":"Textbook combined eastward flow south of the Alaskan Stream, from 30°N to some 200 km off the Alaskan coast; exact longitude support and paired flow boundaries unresolved.","section_geometry":null,"section_orientation":"Broad geographic band description; no resolved cross-flow transect or paired velocity edges.","layer":"No fixed depth layer for the broad North Pacific band; adjacent Alaskan Stream upper-kilometer transport context is separate.","time_convention":"Chapter 8 page version March 2005; no observation dates or width climatology assigned. Preface/version-history September 2002 and first edition 1994 are separate publication context.","boundary_rule":"Author describes a broad band of eastward flow more than 2000 km wide; paired velocity cutoff and calculation unresolved.","source_url":"https://ocg.aori.u-tokyo.ac.jp/member/eoka/documents/Tomczak_Godfrey.pdf","source_citation":"Tomczak, M. and J. S. Godfrey, Regional Oceanography: An Introduction, chapter 8 The Pacific Ocean, printed p125 / PDF p135, page version 1.1 March 2005; original 1994 Pergamon edition, university-hosted online compilation.","source_locator":"Printed p125 / PDF p135, paragraph beginning No transport estimates, North Pacific passage and alternative Subarctic split discussion; adjacent pp124–126 / PDF pp134–136. PDF pp2,7–9 version/preface/authorship.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-09","source_evidence_kind":"textbook_original_broad_combined_flow_synthesis","extraction_method":"More-than qualifier and combined-flow definition transcribed from visually inspected original textbook page; no map or velocity boundary digitization.","whole_current_representative":false,"width_rank_eligible":false,"full_width_inference_eligible":false,"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"seasonal_playback_eligible":false,"is_confidence_i