 depth control and source-estimated sinking about 230 m over 21 months. No fixed numerical width layer.","time_convention":"Table 2 historical composite label January 1989-October 1990, overlapping three unequal subsets. No exact width observation dates or recurring seasonal calendar extracted.","boundary_rule":"Width between zero-velocity points in the composite along-boundary velocity profile, flanked by weak counterflow/recirculation; 10 km averaging bins do not supply a width error.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/93JC00051","source_citation":"Richardson, P. L. and Schmitz, W. J., Jr. (1993), Deep Cross-Equatorial Flow in the Atlantic Measured With SOFAR Floats, Journal of Geophysical Research 98(C5), 8371-8387, doi:10.1029/93JC00051.","source_locator":"Final original PDF p5 / printed p8375, section 3.2 continuation; Table 2 PDF p8 / p8378; nominal depth and processing p2; subset sampling p6 and Figure 6 p7.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-09","source_evidence_kind":"published_original_lagrangian_velocity_composite","extraction_method":"Visually reviewed numerical passage, Table 2 and methods transcribed; no plot-edge digitization or raw velocity recalculation.","whole_current_representative":false,"width_rank_eligible":false,"full_width_inference_eligible":false,"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"seasonal_playback_eligible":false,"is_confidence_interval":false,"phase_label":"Historical upper-core float composite","phase_kind":"lagrangian_composite_zero_velocity_width","observed_period":null,"calendar_months":null,"fixed_layer_bounds_m":null,"uncertainty_km":null,"source_quality_note":"Composite and subset sampling are sparse and nonuniform. Nominal float depths drifted. Source-label and count inconsistencies are preserved; velocity/transport standard errors are not width errors.","remaining_gates":["Acquire and reprocess raw calibrated float records with their changing depths.","Recover geographically supported zero-velocity edges before footprints or physical state intersections.","Repeated compatible sections and width errors before annual margins or seasonal playback.","Independent scientific admission."],"width_metric_label":"Zero-velocity width of along-isobath float composite","original_regional_context":{"description_kind":"dwbc_upper_core_float_composite","width_passage_visually_inspected":true,"underlying_width_methods_reviewed":true,"full_study_reproduced":false,"temporal_operator":"nonuniform_historical_lagrangian_composite","nominal_float_depth_m":1800,"nominal_depth_is_fixed_layer":false,"source_estimated_float_sinking_m":230,"averaging_bin_km":10,"bin_size_is_width_uncertainty":false,"velocity_errors_are_width_uncertainty":false,"transport_errors_are_width_uncertainty":false,"geographic_edges_extracted":false,"map_buffer_eligible":false,"cross_current_width_inheritance_eligible":false,"seasonal_calendar_extracted":false,"source_table_rows":[{"period_label":"Composite: Jan 1989-Oct 1990","current_width_km":100,"floats_in_current":8,"observations_in_current":500,"peak_individual_velocity_range_cm_s":[50,60],"maximum_bin_average_velocity_cm_s":26,"maximum_bin_average_standard_error_cm_s":5,"transport_per_unit_depth_10_3_m2_s":14,"transport_per_unit_depth_standard_error_10_3_m2_s":3,"total_volume_transport_sv":15},{"period_label":"Jan 1989-Oct 1989","current_width_km":100,"floats_in_current":4,"observations_in_current":124,"peak_individual_velocity_range_cm_s":[50,60],"maximum_bin_average_velocity_cm_s":39,"maximum_bin_average_standard_error_cm_s":5,"transport_per_unit_depth_10_3_m2_s":23,"transport_per_unit_depth_standard_error_10_3_m2_s":4,"total_volume_transport_sv":null,"sampling_qualification":"Table 2 footnote: first subset sampled DWBC January-March 1989, with an offshore data gap between 90 and 130 km; transport may be underestimated and width/transport could be larger. Gap endpoints are not current edges or a width range."},{"period_label":"Nov 1989-Apr 1990","current_width_km":100,"floats_in_current":3,"observations_in_current":188,"peak_individual_velocity_range_cm_s":[40,50],"maximum_bin_average_velocity_cm_s":30,"maximum_bin_average_standard_error_cm_s":4,"transport_per_unit_depth_10_3_m2_s":16,"transport_per_unit_depth_standard_error_10_3_m2_s":3,"total_volume_transport_sv":null},{"period_label":"May 1990-Oct 1990","current_width_km":100,"floats_in_current":3,"observations_in_current":177,"peak_individual_velocity_range_cm_s":[30,40],"maximum_bin_average_velocity_cm_s":19,"maximum_bin_average_standard_error_cm_s":6,"transport_per_unit_depth_10_3_m2_s":8,"transport_per_unit_depth_standard_error_10_3_m2_s":2,"total_volume_transport_sv":null}],"source_table_locator":"Table 2, original PDF p8 / printed p8378","source_scope_discrepancy_note":"Table 2 labels 2 S-12 N west of 43 W; section 3.2 describes 0-7 N and 12 months. Historical composite period labels remain source-specific.","subset_observation_count_sum":489,"composite_observation_count":500,"subset_counts_additive":false,"subset_count_discrepancy_note":"Published subset observation counts 124+188+177 total 489, not composite 500. No adjustment or missing-record explanation inferred.","source_sampling_gap_label":"No floats drifted in the boundary current April-December 1989 (Figure 4 caption).","gap_means_current_absent":false,"independent_subset_width_edges_extracted":false,"source_prose_transport_per_unit_depth_10_3_m2_s":13.8,"alternative_subset_based_transport_standard_error_10_3_m2_s":4,"source_total_volume_transport_unrounded_sv":14.7,"volume_transport_support_note":"Total transport couples float horizontal profile with an independent current-meter profile, assumes elliptical shape and integrates 900-2800 m. These are transport construction bounds, not the width layer.","display_title":"Upper-core float-composite width","display_aria_label":"Deep Western Boundary Current upper-core float composite: approximately 100 kilometres between zero-velocity points. Nominal drifting 1800 m floats, nonuni