ce bound, whole-current envelope or annual range.","geographic_scope":"Riiser-Larsenisen continental shelf/slope, southeastern Weddell Sea; section 2 offshore narrow jet embedded in broader southwestward flow. No exact paired geographic width limits supplied.","section_geometry":null,"section_orientation":"Cross-shelf/slope section context; no exact paired width endpoints or flow-normal orientation diagnosed by OSW.","layer":"Detided LADCP horizontal-current context at 100 m (paragraph 5 and Figure 1). Surface-intensified jet; no uniform vertical width slab inferred. 3000 m isobath describes bottom topography.","time_convention":"One observed section on 23 February 2009; January 31 is separate. Neither the 2010 publication date nor the M6 2017–2021 record dates this jet.","boundary_rule":"Author reports jet narrower than 28 km. Velocity cutoff and paired edges unresolved; peak 28 cm/s and broader-flow speed about 10 cm/s are not boundary thresholds.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1029/2010GL043603","source_citation":"Chavanne, C.P., K.J. Heywood, K.W. Nicholls and I. Fer (2010), Observations of the Antarctic Slope Undercurrent in the southeastern Weddell Sea, Geophysical Research Letters 37, L13601, doi:10.1029/2010GL043603.","source_locator":"Primary publisher indexed text: section 2 Observations paragraph 5; processing paragraph 4; Figure 1/2 captions establish section dates and 100 m horizontal-current context.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-14","source_evidence_kind":"published_primary_indexed_dated_jet_width_constraint","extraction_method":"Reported qualifier, reference scale and date transcribed from primary publisher indexed body/captions; original PDF/pixels and fields not acquired or digitized.","whole_current_representative":false,"width_rank_eligible":false,"full_width_inference_eligible":false,"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"seasonal_playback_eligible":false,"is_confidence_interval":false,"phase_label":"Riiser-Larsenise