ion_orientation":"Width along a baseline bearing135 degrees true; transport velocity is the component normal to that baseline. Recorded flow directions vary; no exact flow-normal projection applied.","layer":"Transport per unit width integrated from surface to local bottom, with variable bathymetry. No fixed-depth width layer or surface-only speed boundary.","time_convention":"Three complete crossings1,3,4:30June–5July,11–15July,16–18July1967. Campaign26June–18July is separate. Multi-day occupations, not simultaneous snapshots or continuous monthly/seasonal means; source clock timezone unspecified.","boundary_rule":"Authors smooth transport-per-unit-width measurements and extend their curves to zero. No negative inshore transport was observed; inshore edges are extrapolated. Two complete crossings have offshore negative values, one offshore edge is also extended to zero.","source_url":"https://www2.whoi.edu/staff/prichardson/wp-content/uploads/sites/75/2018/11/Richardson-Knauss-1971-dsr.pdf","source_citation":"Richardson, P. L. and Knauss, J. A. (1971), Gulf Stream and Western Boundary Undercurrent observations at Cape Hatteras, Deep-Sea Research18,1089–1109, doi:10.1016/0011-7471(71)90095-7.","source_locator":"Methods printed1091/PDF3; Fig2 printed1093/PDF5; zero-edge construction printed1094–1095/PDF6–7; Table2 printed1105/PDF17; mean135 km printed1107/PDF19.","source_evidence_kind":"published_original_transport_float_campaign_statistics","extraction_method":"Transcribed explicit author widths and mean; matched complete occupations using Figure2 and Table2. No curve digitization, geographic endpoints or width error inferred.","phase_label":"1967 three complete crossings · zero-transport spans","phase_kind":"campaign_width_statistics","observed_period":{"start":"1967-06-30","end":"1967-07-18"},"source_quality_note":"Inshore zero boundaries are author extrapolations, not observed sign reversals. Multi-day sampling and changing flow direction limit synoptic/flow-normal interpretation. Baseline135 degrees differs from mean135 km.","remaining_gates":["Recover geographic boundary coordinates and the original transport observations.","Quantify section-orientation, interpolation and sampling uncertainty.","Independent scientific admission before whole-current dimensions or annual variability."],"original_regional_context":{"description_kind":"gulf_stream_transport_float_complete_crossing_statistics","complete_crossing_occupations":[{"id":"gulf-stream-1967-crossing-1","crossing_number":1,"observed_period":{"start":"1967-06-30","end":"1967-07-05"},"width_km":145,"transport_sv":58,"source_clock_timezone":null,"is_synoptic_snapshot":false},{"id":"gulf-stream-1967-crossing-3","crossing_number":3,"observed_period":{"start":"1967-07-11","end":"1967-07-15"},"width_km":140,"transport_sv":67,"source_clock_timezone":null,"is_synoptic_snapshot":false},{"id":"gulf-stream-1967-crossing-4","crossing_number":4,"observed_period":{"start":"1967-07-16","end":"1967-07-18"},"width_km":120,"transport_sv":64,"source_clock_timezone":null,"is_synoptic_snapshot":false}],"partial_crossing_without_width":2,"reported_mean_width_km":135,"mean_is_independent_occupation":false,"campaign_context_period":{"start":"1967-06-26","end":"1967-07-18"},"baseline_bearing_degrees_true":135,"baseline_bearing_is_width":false,"width_is_exact_flow_normal_projection":false,"author_boundary_extrapolation_present":true,"inshore_negative_transport_observed":false,"offshore_negative_transport_observed_complete_crossing_count":2,"all_paired_edges_observed_sign_reversals":false,"source_curve_or_coordinates_digitized":false,"occupation_range_is_uncertainty_or_annual_extrema":false,"display_aria_label":"Gulf Stream off Cape Hatteras: three author zero-transport section widths145,140,120 km in1967; reported mean135 km and finite sample span120–145 km. Author extrapolation is retained; no annual extrema or geographic edges.","display_caption":"Mean135 km; three complete1967 crossings span1