ational section to an OSW 5 E pre-island approach gate. Excludes western North Brazil retroflection source paths, island bifurcation near 6 E, downstream branches and westward returns. Not full source-to-termination length or an observed material trajectory.","route_extent_kind":"35 W to pre-island equatorial reach","approximate_reference_path_km":4500,"scenario_range_km":[4300,4600],"scenario_count":81,"source_url":"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/2022-11/010086132.pdf","source_locator":"Introduction pp. 1–2: eastward equatorial flow, eastern bifurcation/termination-site context between 5 E and continental margin, Sao Tome around 6.6 E; sections 2–3 distinguish observations and model experiments.","supporting_sources":[{"url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2006JC003931","citation":"Hormann and Brandt (2007), Atlantic Equatorial Undercurrent and associated cold tongue variability, JGR Oceans, doi:10.1029/2006JC003931.","locator":"Section 2.3.1.1 paragraph 14: observed 35 W current centered at equator with approximately 100 m core; paragraphs 16–18 distinguish 23 W and subsurface currents.","role":"Western observational section gate and layer/context distinction; no transport-to-length or depth-uniform inference."}],"candidate_file":"research/atlantic-euc-reach-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"1256ace4b349ed71d251f4f30f4a7296a7b137641d855c795538b05d41337974","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","figure":"figures/atlantic-euc-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["ETRA","GUIN","WTRA"],"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_C_4","remaining_gates":["Review 35 W and pre-island truncation; source retroflections and eastern branches are not represented.","Obtain compatible depth/time-resolved velocity axis before physical length or seasonal dimensions.","Resolve island interaction and return-flow topology without treating gener