ation; no drifter axis digitized."},{"url":"https://accedacris.ulpgc.es/bitstream/10553/52759/1/azores_current_system_from.pdf","citation":"Comas-Rodriguez et al. (2011), The Azores Current System from a meridional section at 24.5 W, JGR Oceans 116, C09021, doi:10.1029/2011JC007129.","locator":"Abstract and section 2: 2009 meridional survey; 110 km widths and separate eastward/westward currents.","role":"Section context only; width is not along-current length and is not applied along the route."}],"candidate_file":"research/azores-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"67aa89df57823098ed8b80cd06f93113847335ea6af5b0c68b6f5e7eb799ad8c","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","figure":"figures/azores-reference-path-candidate.svg","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["CNRY","NADR","NAST E","NAST W","NWCS"],"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_C_2","remaining_gates":["Review Grand Banks branching and offshore eastern approach naming gates before length admission.","Validate intermediate jet corridor, bathymetry and finer geography using suitable velocity fields; no measured axis extracted.","Keep countercurrent and southward recirculation branches separate; neither widths nor branch lengths transferred.","Obtain consistent dated geometry and width boundaries before seasonal playback or annual length/width ranges.","Canonical admission and publication review."],"parent_current_id":null,"parent_scope_note":null,"ordering_sensitivity":{"overlapping_candidate_ids":["north-atlantic-reference-path-candidate","brazil-reference-path-candidate"],"envelope_position_bounds":[3,5],"interpretation":"Conservative positions within retained rounded route envelopes, treating choices independently; touching envelopes overlap. Not a statistical rank interval or a uniform whole-current comparison."}},{"id":"agulhas-return-reach-reference-path-candidate","current_id":"agulhas-return","name":"Agulhas Return Current","status":"editorial_refer