omponent through central Great Australian Bight). Paragraphs 57–58 name downstream components separately.","supporting_sources":[],"candidate_file":"research/leeuwin-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"fa33d759c41494c5db7cd06bda58f4e7d74e8dc373dd3f7f54b4314d08dbc239","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","figure":"figures/leeuwin-reference-path-candidate.svg","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["ARCH","AUSW"],"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_F_5","remaining_gates":["Scientific review of Leeuwin naming/penetration conventions and the eastern gate.","Check offshore route against reproducible bathymetric or layer-specific velocity geometry.","Canonical admission and publication review; preserve the separate published lower bound and 5,500 km system estimate."],"parent_current_id":null,"parent_scope_note":null,"ordering_sensitivity":{"overlapping_candidate_ids":["brazil-reference-path-candidate","caribbean-reference-path-candidate","east-greenland-reference-path-candidate","benguela-reference-path-candidate","north-brazil-reference-path-candidate","labrador-reference-path-candidate","hiri-reference-path-candidate"],"envelope_position_bounds":[5,12],"interpretation":"Conservative positions within retained rounded route envelopes, treating choices independently; touching envelopes overlap. Not a statistical rank interval or a uniform whole-current comparison."}},{"id":"atlantic-seuc-reach-reference-path-candidate","current_id":"atlantic-south-equatorial-undercurrent","name":"Atlantic South Equatorial Undercurrent","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","comparison_group":"osw_studied_reach_routes","scope":"Declared western-to-central Atlantic subsurface reach from the 35 W section near 3 S to an OSW truncation near 10 W, 4.3 S. Uses the published float-study domain, not full-current start and termination. Excludes westward SEC legs, NBUC source pathways, recirculation loops, s