ank interval or a uniform whole-current comparison."}},{"id":"norwegian-coastal-reference-path-candidate","current_id":"norwegian-coastal","name":"Norwegian Coastal Current","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","comparison_group":"osw_approximate_reference_routes","scope":"OSW southern Norwegian Skagerrak approach to the Ingoy section at the Barents Sea entrance, following a simplified offshore coastal corridor. Excludes Baltic source-water transit, Jutland inflow, fjord circuits, offshore Norwegian Atlantic Current branches, West Spitsbergen and downstream Murman continuation. No whole connected-system length.","route_extent_kind":"Norwegian coastal corridor to Ingoy","approximate_reference_path_km":2100,"scenario_range_km":[2000,2200],"scenario_count":54,"source_url":"https://gmd.copernicus.org/articles/19/2785/2026/","source_locator":"Section 1 Introduction: Norwegian Coastal Current originates in Skagerrak and flows along Norway into Barents Sea; explicitly distinguished from warm saline Norwegian Atlantic Current.","supporting_sources":[{"url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2011JC006996","citation":"Skagseth, Drinkwater and Terrile (2011), Wind- and buoyancy-induced transport of the Norwegian Coastal Current in the Barents Sea, JGR Oceans 116, doi:10.1029/2011JC006996.","locator":"Introduction paragraphs 3-7 and Figure 2: source-water convention, coastal route and complex Tromsoflaket pathways converging near Ingoy; data section distinguishes local measurements.","role":"Ingoy gate context and continuity caveat; no drifter trajectory or velocity field digitized."}],"candidate_file":"research/norwegian-coastal-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"58515d8bc8ba54f98c3b9be3fe2827195d0bfec3a559461a3f2d0db11961841e","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","figure":"figures/norwegian-coastal-reference-path-candidate.svg","nominal_atlas_state_cros