easternmost RAFOS reach near 43 S, 16 W; large meanders and possible SAC/ACC exchange. Figure 11 is context only, not digitized.","supporting_sources":[],"candidate_file":"research/south-atlantic-reach-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"7f6258f70942eead02f9c621b13b32db7effb641901e4933b50cbb51338647f2","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","figure":"figures/south-atlantic-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["BRAZ","SATL"],"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_C_5","remaining_gates":["Validate source anchor interpretation, depth and regional naming independently; the farthest observed float reach is not a whole-current endpoint.","Acquire dated float or suitable velocity geometry before measuring physical meander length; do not transfer this reach to the surface current.","Resolve eastern-basin continuation, SAC/ACC exchange and recirculation before a full-current length.","Keep all annual dimensions and physical width unresolved; complete canonical measurement and publication review separately."],"parent_current_id":null,"parent_scope_note":null,"ordering_sensitivity":null},{"id":"agulhas-reference-path-candidate","current_id":"agulhas","name":"Agulhas Current","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","comparison_group":"osw_approximate_reference_routes","scope":"Regional southward Agulhas reference route from 27 degrees S to a 40 degrees S retroflection gate near 19 degrees E. Includes an editorial approach to the turning region; stops before the eastward Agulhas Return Current. Excludes upstream Mozambique/East Madagascar branches, leakage and ring trajectories. This is a regional extent convention, not the narrower coastal-jet definition or whole Agulhas system.","route_extent_kind":"regional extent to retroflection","approximate_reference_path_km":2000,"scenario_range_km":[1800,2200],"scenario_count":81,"source_url":"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2022.837906/full","source_locator":"Regional and Shelf-Scale / The Agulhas Current System: regional 27–40 degrees S description, retroflection at 18–20 degrees E and eastward return-current distinction; broader/early retroflections discussed separately.","supporting_sources":[],"candidate_file":"research/agulhas-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"2b5a04d3b3a21029c61ffb96001080746ae8667be6eff3a1cabf59e56c1b2acc","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","figure":"figures/agulhas-reference-path-candidate.svg","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["EAFR","SSTC"],"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_D_5","remaining_gates":["Independent review of regional extent versus coastal-jet naming and the retroflection/return handoff.","Validate offshore waypoints against reproducible bathymetric or velocity geometry; extend endpoint scenarios if warranted.","Canonical geometry/measurement integration and publication review before admission."],"parent_current_id":null,"parent_scope_note":null,"ordering_sensitivity":{"overlapping_candidate_ids":["benguela-reference-path-candidate","north-brazil-reference-path-candidate","black-sea-rim-reference-path-candidate","east-australian-reference-path-candidate","labrador-reference-path-candidate","norwegian-coastal-reference-path-candidate","hiri-reference-path-candidate","canary-reference-path-candidate","somali-winter-reference-path-candidate","portugal-reference-path-candidate"],"envelope_position_bounds":[9,19],"interpretation":"Conservative positions within retained rounded route envelopes, treating choices independently; touching envelopes overlap. Not a statistical rank interval or a uniform whole-current comparison."}},{"id":"hiri-reference-path-candidate","current_id":"hiri-current","name":"Hiri Current","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","comparison_group":"osw_approximate_reference_routes","scope":"Broad Hiri naming convention: northward Australian boundary branch from an OSW 15 S bifurcation approach, clockwise around the Gulf of Papua entrance, to an OSW eastern Louisiade approach. Excludes closed gyre return circuits, direct mid-basin Solomon inflow, EAC, downstream New Guinea currents and eddy excursions. Narrower literature uses Hiri only south of PNG and proposes Gulf of Papua Current for the connected boundary system; no alias merge or complete system extent admitted.","route_extent_kind":"broad Hiri regional route","approximate_reference_path_km":1900,"scenario_range_km":[1900,2500],"scenario_count":54,"source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2017JC013221","source_locator":"Section 1 and section 3.1.5: northward branch initiated near 15 S, clockwise Gulf of Papua circulation and depth dependence. Figure 1 separates upper 0-300 m and deeper modeled flows.","supporting_sources":[{"url":"https://absa.asn.au/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/Cor-Vol-17-Pg135-145_CoralSeaCurrents.pdf","citation":"Burrage (1993), Coral Sea Currents, Corella 17(5), 135-145.","locator":"Introduction, printed pp. 136-137: northward branch around Gulf entrance, exit around Louisiades and broad Hiri naming.","role":"Regional path topology only; hydrographic figures not digitized."},{"url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/2013JC009591","citation":"Oliver and Holbrook (2014), Extending our understanding of South Pacific gyre spin-up: Modeling the East Australian Current in a future climate, doi:10.1002/2013JC009591.","locator":"Section 3: regional SEC bifurcation near 18 S and northward Hiri naming.","role":"Alternative regional origin convention, not a current-core track."},{"url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/2013JC009678","citation":"Ganachaud et al. (2014), The Southwest Pacific Ocean circulation and climate experiment (SPICE), doi:10.1002/2013JC009678.","locator":"Section 4.1: NQC, GBRUC a