pstream Azores/Portugal routes, the broader Iberian-to-tropical Canary Current System, Lanzarote Passage recirculation, poleward undercurrents and downstream North Equatorial Current. No whole connected-system length.","route_extent_kind":"Canary offshore return-flow corridor","approximate_reference_path_km":1700,"scenario_range_km":[1500,1800],"scenario_count":54,"source_url":"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/14/971/2018/","source_locator":"Section 1 Introduction, first paragraph: distinguishes approximately 35-20 N named-current region from wider Canary Current System; bifurcation away from Africa near Cape Blanc (21 N) toward the North Equatorial Current.","supporting_sources":[{"url":"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/22/2059/2026/","citation":"Ibrahim and Sun (2026), A multidecadal sea level rise and its hiatus in the tropical Atlantic margin off northwest Africa, Ocean Science 22, 2059-2081, doi:10.5194/os-22-2059-2026.","locator":"Section 4 opening paragraphs: source-region convergence around 35 N and upper-layer context.","role":"Northern geographic naming-gate context; no model axis digitized."},{"url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2022JC019487","citation":"Perez-Hernandez et al. (2023), The Seasonal Cycle of the Eastern Boundary Currents of the North Atlantic Subtropical Gyre, JGR Oceans 128, e2022JC019487.","locator":"Abstract and sections 1-2: regional seasonal migration and distinct Lanzarote Passage flow; Table 1 and prose disagree about fall cruise month.","role":"Seasonal continuity caveat; no 2015 observed axis, section width, transport or annual extrema reconstructed."}],"candidate_file":"research/canary-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"b5a8dad9c074d00432e07cb45640469551f1686d3b96e31a4356d0861c7c4309","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","figure":"figures/canary-reference-path-candidate.svg","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["CNRY"],"recommended_nasa_ti