 Current","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","comparison_group":"osw_studied_reach_routes","scope":"Declared 103 W to 88 W eastern regional studied reach between two reported Subtropical Front crossings associated with the SPC in the source regional surface circulation. Front locations are proxies, not diagnosed velocity-core endpoints, and were observed in different years. OSW connecting vertices and alternatives are editorial. Branch correspondence is unresolved. Excludes Chatham Rise/western basin, ACC export branch, Peru-Chile coastal flow, northward recirculation and independent split bands. Not a whole-current or simultaneous observed axis.","route_extent_kind":"STF-proxy regional reach","approximate_reference_path_km":1400,"scenario_range_km":[1300,1500],"scenario_count":27,"source_url":"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/2024-12/010047303.pdf","source_locator":"Chaigneau and Pizarro (2005), Data [4]–[5], surface circulation [7], STF [14]–[17] and Table 1: P18 at 103 W 33.8 S and P19 at 88 W 34.5 S. Source front/velocity distinction retained; fields and curves not digitized.","supporting_sources":[{"url":"https://journals.ametsoc.org/view/journals/phoc/25/1/1520-0485_1995_025_0077_tspc_2_0_co_2.xml","citation":"Stramma, Peterson and Tomczak (1995), The South Pacific Current, JPO 25, 77–91.","locator":"Publisher-indexed abstract; direct article/PDF access unsuccessful.","supports":"SPC distinction from ACC, broad Chatham Rise context and possible splitting at 115–85 W. Does not assign a branch to this connection."},{"url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2007GL030392","citation":"Ridgway and Dunn (2007), Observational evidence for a Southern Hemisphere oceanic supergyre, GRL 34, L13612.","locator":"Section 3.4 [15]: gyre return flow and STF relation.","supports":"Layered gyre return flow is not universally identified by the STF; no whole-current or intermediate-layer axis copied from surface/frontal proxies."}],"candidate_file":"research/south-pacific-eastern-front-reach-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"8f5450e07b3d47867d57289d7bafddb502ab8b8b7f5c27d8fb67b1485f4fcedb","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","figure":"figures/south-pacific-eastern-front-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["HUMB"],"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_A_5","remaining_gates":["Diagnose a same-layer velocity axis; frontal proxy locations are not current-core locations.","Recover compatible simultaneous observations before a dated route or seasonal extrema.","Resolve two-band correspondence within the 115–85 W split region described by Stramma et al. (1995).","Test front-to-flow correspondence against the layered supergyre distinction in Ridgway and Dunn (2007).","Resolve western and eastern continuation independently before a whole-current length or annual width."],"parent_current_id":null,"parent_scope_note":null,"ordering_sensitivity":null},{"id":"atlantic-neuc-reach-reference-path-candidate","current_id":"atlantic-north-equatorial-undercurrent","name":"Atlantic North Equatorial Undercurrent","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","comparison_group":"osw_studied_reach_routes","scope":"Declared western-to-central Atlantic subsurface reference reach between observations at 35 W near 5 N and the central observational neighborhood at 23 W near 5 N. Connecting vertices are editorial, not an observed continuous axis. Excludes NBC/NEC source recirculation, surface NECC flow, uncertain filaments east of 28 W and farther-east termination. Not full-current source-to-end length.","route_extent_kind":"35 W–23 W subsurface reference reach","approximate_reference_path_km":1300,"scenario_range_km":[1200,1400],"scenario_count":81,"source_url":"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/pleins_textes_7/b_fdi_51-52/010019670.pdf","source_locator":"Bourles et al. (1999), section 4.8, p. 21163: 35 W NEUC centered at 5 N in February 1993 and April 1996; core near sigma-theta 26.75. Sections 4.6 and 6.1 separate source retroflection from the named current; eastern filament context cites earlier work.","supporting_sources":[{"url":"https://pureadmin.uhi.ac.uk/ws/portalfiles/portal/14119479/2020GL088350.pdf","citation":"Burmeister, Luebbecke, Brandt, Claus and Hahn (2020), Fluctuations of the Atlantic North Equatorial Undercurrent and Associated Changes in Oxygen Transports, GRL 47, e2020GL088350, doi:10.1029/2020GL088350.","locator":"Introduction and sections 2–4, pp. 1–4: central 5 N, 23 W observations and 65–270 m definition; data intervals and fixed-box/inferred-transport distinctions.","role":"Central observational context; weak seasonal cycle and episodic intraseasonal events do not establish seasonal geometry."},{"url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2018JC014760","citation":"Burmeister, Luebbecke, Brandt and Duteil (2019), Interannual Variability of the Atlantic North Equatorial Undercurrent and Its Impact on Oxygen, JGR Oceans 124, 2348–2373, doi:10.1029/2018JC014760.","locator":"Introduction, sections 2.1 and 2.3: 23 W ship sections; model half-width and observational integration boundaries.","role":"Distinguishes chosen transport integration widths and model-domain longitude span from diagnosed current dimensions."}],"candidate_file":"research/atlantic-neuc-reach-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"386796f3f152bc36828c6f3a1c88f262f9f8a054c1f2f3465839dae252af34ca","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","figure":"figures/atlantic-neuc-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["WTRA"],"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_C_3","remaining_gates":["Diagnose a compatible subsurface axis before asserting continuity across the separate section neighborhoods.","Resolve source recirculation, eastern filaments and termination before whole-current length.","Review historical two-degree latitude width with boundary and month-date precision support; no whole width or seasonal range inferred.","Keep mooring transport variability distinct from seasonal length/width geometry."],"parent_current_id":null,"parent_scope_note":null,"ordering_sensitivity":null},{"id":"davidson-winter-reference-path-candidate","current_id":"davidson","name":"Davidson Current","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","comparison_group":"osw_approximate_reference_routes","scope":"California-Oregon winter coastal reference corridor between OSW gates at 35 N and 46 N. These are bookkeeping gates, not source-published current endpoints. Excludes conditional Vancouver Island penetration and the deeper California Undercurrent. No full-system length or width footprint.","route_extent_kind":"historical winter regional corridor","approximate_reference_path_km":1300,"scenario_range_km":[1200,1400],"scenario_count":54,"source_url":"https://waves-vagues.dfo-mpo.gc.ca/library-bibliotheque/40591190_v2.pdf","source_locator":"Appendix II section II.1, printed II-1 to II-2 / PDF pages 12-13: northward seasonal surface strip along California and Oregon from October to March; Vancouver Island penetration is conditional.","supporting_sources":[],"candidate_file":"research/davidson-winter-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"ac2db281859e27e8903fb224f3fdde35b36f010ab111240e2a2c78e3c5a26609","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","figure":"figures/davidson-winter-reference-path-candidate.svg","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["CCAL","OCAL"],"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_A_2","remaining_gates":["Review source observational basis, current boundaries and historical applicability.","Validate coastal vertices and named-flow gates using bathymetry and suitable winter velocity fields.","No conditional Vancouve