nvelopes overlap. Not a statistical rank interval or a uniform whole-current comparison."}},{"id":"algerian-reference-path-candidate","current_id":"algerian","name":"Algerian Current","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","comparison_group":"osw_approximate_reference_routes","scope":"Eastward Algerian coastal regional reference route from an OSW Alboran-transition gate to an OSW eastern Algeria gate. Alternative later western and earlier eastern gates test regional extent. Excludes Alboran gyres, detached Algerian eddies and downstream Sardinia-channel or other Mediterranean circulation. Source does not define exact terminal coordinates or whole-system termination.","route_extent_kind":"Algerian coastal regional route","approximate_reference_path_km":900,"scenario_range_km":[600,900],"scenario_count":108,"source_url":"https://essd.copernicus.org/articles/11/147/2019/","source_locator":"Cotroneo et al. (2019), section 1: after leaving the Alboran Sea, Atlantic Water flows eastward along the Algerian coast in an along-slope Algerian Current; the study surveys the Algerian Basin, not the complete named-current axis.","supporting_sources":[],"candidate_file":"research/algerian-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"5d6ee850599ff09dec79a0ce84654712f5aefdd19bc91c1ff53a29178fc8d651","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","figure":"figures/algerian-reference-path-candidate.svg","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["MEDI"],"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_C_2","remaining_gates":["Scientific review of named-flow gates and regional scope.","Verify shelf/slope correspondence with reproducible bathymetry or suitable velocity data.","Canonical admission and publication review; these are editorial route lengths."],"parent_current_id":null,"parent_scope_note":null,"ordering_sensitivity":{"overlapping_candidate_ids":["alaska-reference-path-candidate","irminger-reference-path-candidate","west