east South America.","role":"Current identity and direction only; no source-defined endpoints or numeric length."},{"url":"https://www.fao.org/4/x6078e/x6078e00.htm","citation":"IMR/NORAD/UNDP/FAO report front matter, November 1989.","locator":"Report title, publication date, chapter attribution and electronic OCR notice.","role":"Survey and publication provenance; OCR limits remain explicit."}],"candidate_file":"research/guiana-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"fa12de259d0401bb677ca369a3f15a0a482d73542561116587f7e161285ff22b","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","figure":"figures/guiana-reference-path-candidate.svg","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["GUIA"],"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_B_3","remaining_gates":["Review regional scope and selected offshore vertices against original survey charts and suitable bathymetry; coarse land clearance is insufficient.","Resolve Guiana versus North Brazil naming conventions and dated continuity before estimating whole-current length.","Do not infer a modern velocity axis, freshwater-plume edge, current polygon or physical OSW state passage from this editorial corridor.","Seasonal geometry, length variation, width and annual extrema remain unsupported by this geographic route.","Scientific and canonical admission review; retain studied-reach exclusion from the whole-current reference-route order."],"parent_current_id":null,"parent_scope_note":null,"ordering_sensitivity":null},{"id":"solomon-island-coastal-undercurrent-reference-path-candidate","current_id":"solomon-island-coastal-undercurrent","name":"Solomon Island Coastal Undercurrent","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","comparison_group":"osw_studied_reach_routes","scope":"Editorial eastern Solomon Islands reach between offshore gates near 162.0 E, 9.6 S and 155.8 E, 4.6 S, following island-chain geography toward northeast Bougainville. Excludes the SEC upstream basin, Solomon Strait crossing, New Ireland coastal continuation and EUC. Source descriptions establish regional context; continuity between gates is unresolved. These are OSW truncations, not observed origins or termination.","route_extent_kind":"eastern Solomon Islands reference reach","approximate_reference_path_km":900,"scenario_range_km":[800,1000],"scenario_count":81,"source_url":"https://faculty.washington.edu/kessler/abstracts/melet_etal_2010.html","source_locator":"Melet et al. (2010) coauthor abstract proposes SICU east of Solomon Islands; original model axis not acquired. Ganachaud et al. (2017), Figures 2 and 7 and pages 11-12/17, supply island geography and local observational context, not a continuous SICU axis.","supporting_sources":[{"label":"Ganachaud et al. (2017), Solomon Sea cruises","url":"https://doi.org/10.1525/elementa.221","locator":"Figures 2 and 7; pages 5-7, 11-12 and 17","access":"Original NOAA-hosted PDF acquired and institutional SHA256 matched; CC BY 4.0 printed page 27; selected pages and figures inspected."}],"candidate_file":"research/solomon-island-coastal-undercurrent-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"64c8f36d57216f978f94ed81debd6f4d8d95b74c985ee613870c3a41d2c7942d","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","figure":"figures/solomon-island-coastal-undercurrent-reference-path-candidate.svg","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["AUSE","WARM"],"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_G_4","remaining_gates":["Acquire and visually review the original 2010 model Figure 4 before digitizing a model axis.","Review finer coastline and bathymetry, source velocity fields and the density-dependent flow before identifying an actual current core.","Resolve complete entrance/exit gates and connectivity to NICU separately; no connector across Solomon Strait is drawn.","No whole-current width, annual range, dated footprint or NASA surface identification inferred."],"parent_current_id":null,"parent_scope_note":null,"ordering_sensitivity":null},{"id":"east-adriatic-reference-path-candidate","current_id":"east-adriatic","name":"East Adriatic Current","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","comparison_group":"osw_approximate_reference_routes","scope":"OSW offshore eastern-Adriatic reference corridor under the Otranto-to-Istria surface-circulation convention. Gates are editorial neighborhoods, not observed origins or termination. Excludes western return flow, sub-basin recirculation loops and unverified island-channel branches. The possible Dalmatian-name overlap is unresolved and its extent is not transferred. The published 800 km basin length is not used as current length; this estimate comes from the declared OSW vertices.","route_extent_kind":"Otranto-Istria surface-circulation convention","approximate_reference_path_km":800,"scenario_range_km":[700,800],"scenario_count":81,"source_url":"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/14/1461/2018/","source_locator":"Sciascia et al. (2018), Section 2.1 and Figure 1 caption: northwestward eastern Balkan coast circulation, separate western return and three sub-basin gyres. Endpoint convention from Urbini et al. (2020), Study Area, circulation paragraph.","supporting_sources":[{"url":"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2020.00679/full","citation":"Urbini et al. (2020), Temporal and Spatial Variability of the CO2 System in a Riverine Influenced Area of the Mediterranean Sea, the Northern Adriatic, doi:10.3389/fmars.2020.00679.","locator":"Study Area, general circulation paragraph: eastern-side northward flow from Otranto toward Istrian Peninsula, citing Poulain (2001).","role":"Regional endpoint convention; not a measured continuous current axis or named termination."}],"candidate_file":"research/east-adriatic-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"f4aa14b11d2109ab8df178538e0b954f8431bff833b763fa868f9ba874041455","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075