st Greenland continuation. Not the full EGCC or the source-reported approximately 1000 km surveyed shelf. Near 63 N, the coastal and shelfbreak flows approach or merge; the line does not establish uninterrupted independent coastal flow. The local 30 km Cape Farewell width is not a buffer around this reach.","route_extent_kind":"66 N–Cape Farewell studied reach","approximate_reference_path_km":800,"scenario_range_km":[800,900],"scenario_count":81,"source_url":"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/Sutherland_EGCC_revised_withfigs_33743.pdf","source_locator":"Sutherland and Pickart (2008), section 3: Cape Farewell and 66 N section geography; section 3.5: weak assumed northern jet near 68 N; sections 8-9: merging near 63 N and approximately 1000 km shelf survey description. Relevant text inspected, no current-axis figure digitized.","supporting_sources":[],"candidate_file":"research/east-greenland-coastal-reach-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"606edd4cfe959e577c65a0a089b607006ed878823af280f113bba682da6af680","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","figure":"figures/east-greenland-coastal-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["SARC"],"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_B_1","remaining_gates":["Review finer coastline and shelf bathymetry before claiming an inner-shelf current axis.","Resolve northern identification and the 63 N merger before any whole-current extent.","Do not replace the source approximately 1000 km shelf survey description with this shorter editorial reach.","Retain the Cape Farewell 30 km threshold width as a local section; no width buffer or annual footprint inferred."],"parent_current_id":null,"parent_scope_note":null,"ordering_sensitivity":null},{"id":"monsoon-summer-sri-lanka-reference-path-candidate","current_id":"monsoon","name":"Monsoon Current","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","comparison_group":"osw_studied_reach_routes","scope":"Declared 77–83 E Sri Lanka regional summer reach, oriented eastward. Gates and connecting vertices are selected by OSW; neither gate is a physical whole-current endpoint. Excludes Arabian Sea source branches, Laccadive circulation, Bay of Bengal continuation, equatorial jets and subsurface counterflows. Different seasonal drawings do not diagnose occupied footprints or annual extrema.","route_extent_kind":"summer regional reach","approximate_reference_path_km":800,"scenario_range_km":[700,900],"scenario_count":27,"source_url":"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/schott_mccreary_41948.pdf","source_locator":"Schott and McCreary (2001), section 5.1.5, printed pp. 63–65 / PDF indices 62–64: seasonal directions/months, Sri Lanka bottleneck and separate upper-layer/undercurrent flows. August 1993 and January 1991 sections provide local latitude context, not regional axis vertices.","supporting_sources":[],"candidate_file":"research/monsoon-summer-sri-lanka-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"1074de5de5d68f6ca753a8eafdb2fea5eaecd20204f008c6df156e3c21940f92","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","figure":"figures/monsoon-summer-sri-lanka-reference-path-candidate.svg","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["MONS"],"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_E_3","remaining_gates":["Review the regional gate/axis choices against compatible seasonal velocity fields.","Separate surface flow, near-coastal counterflow, equatorial jets and undercurrents.","Resolve upstream and downstream branches before a whole-current estimate.","Recover matching seasonal transverse boundaries and repeated comparable observations before annual dimensions."],"parent_current_id":null,"parent_scope_note":null,"ordering_sensitivity":null},{"id":"south-australian-reference-path-candidate","current_id":"south-australian","name":"South Australian Current","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","comparison_group":"o