018/","source_locator":"Berta et al. (2018), section 1: formation in the Ligurian Sea, southwestward continental-slope flow recognizable as far as the Catalan Sea. Aguiar et al. (2022), section 2.1: Iberian-slope continuation and bifurcation near 40.6 N.","supporting_sources":[{"url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1029/2021JC017589","citation":"Aguiar et al. (2022), Strong Long-Lived Anticyclonic Mesoscale Eddies in the Balearic Sea: Formation, Intensification, and Thermal Impact, doi:10.1029/2021JC017589.","locator":"Section 2.1, Study Area: Northern Current splits near 40.6 N; one branch continues through Ibiza Channel, another contributes to Balearic Current."}],"candidate_file":"research/northern-mediterranean-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"aa383cd4679ba5f593b9a7ddb29c16edbe08c94138372a680672e5fc61ba6c19","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","figure":"figures/northern-mediterranean-reference-path-candidate.svg","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["MEDI","NECS"],"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_C_2","remaining_gates":["Scientific review of named-flow gates and regional scope.","Verify shelf/slope correspondence with reproducible bathymetry or suitable velocity data.","Canonical admission and publication review; these are editorial route lengths."],"parent_current_id":null,"parent_scope_note":null,"ordering_sensitivity":{"overlapping_candidate_ids":["alaska-reference-path-candidate","irminger-reference-path-candidate","mindanao-reference-path-candidate","oyashio-reference-path-candidate","algerian-reference-path-candidate","east-adriatic-reference-path-candidate","south-australian-reference-path-candidate","west-spitsbergen-reference-path-candidate","zeehan-reference-path-candidate","western-adriatic-reference-path-candidate","somali-summer-southern-reference-path-candidate"],"envelope_position_bounds":[25,36],"interpretation":"Conservative positions within retained rounded route 