rent length, physical width and annual ranges remain unresolved.","No seasonal playback, occupied polygon, physical state containment or NASA current identity inferred."],"parent_current_id":null,"parent_scope_note":null,"ordering_sensitivity":null},{"id":"redsox-northern-plume-reach-reference-path-candidate","current_id":"red-sea-saline-overflow","name":"Red Sea saline overflow - northern plume reference reach","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","comparison_group":"osw_studied_reach_routes","scope":"Declared northern descending-plume regional connection from an OSW Bab-el-Mandeb approach gate toward the Figure 1 lower-channel neighborhood. Every vertex is an independent rounded editorial choice. Excludes the other branch, gully products, late equilibrated-water spreading and a whole-parent length.","route_extent_kind":"northern descending-plume reference reach","approximate_reference_path_km":120,"scenario_range_km":[110,130],"scenario_count":81,"source_url":"https://www2.whoi.edu/site/bower-lab/wp-content/uploads/sites/12/2018/03/Peters_2005_MixingEntrainment.pdf","source_locator":"Peters et al. (2005), section 2, section 3a and Figure 1 printed571 / PDF3 identify two preferred descending plume pathways. Section5a printed575 / PDF7 describes non-synoptic velocity-supported northern reach 130 km; channel lengths / 5 km width are different objects. Source figure inspected for orientation only.","supporting_sources":[],"candidate_file":"research/redsox-northern-plume-reach-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"c5cbd42353d683815c523b611be5fd52f3f6639badc2ae9393c15a5118de5e45","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","figure":"figures/redsox-northern-plume-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["REDS"],"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_D_3","remaining_gates":["Independently validate component/naming,layer,gates,fine coastline and bathymetry before physical admission.","Acquire compatible dated velocity geometry before measuring a current axis or seasonal dimensions.","Do not sum component reaches or transfer neighboring current/channel widths.","Whole-current dimensions,annual ranges,occupied width polygons,physical state containment and NASA identity remain unresolved."],"parent_current_id":null,"parent_scope_note":null,"ordering_sensitivity":null},{"id":"ligurian-reach-reference-path-candidate","current_id":"ligurian","name":"Ligurian Current","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","comparison_group":"osw_studied_reach_routes","scope":"Declared coastal studied reach of the Northern Current from an OSW offshore Genoa neighborhood gate through the Imperia sector to an OSW Menton–Nice neighborhood gate. Ligurian is retained as the ledger regional segment classification, not a separate additive current system. Excludes Corsica feeder routes, basin-wide drifter loops and downstream Provencal/Catalan continuation. Gates are not whole-current endpoints.","route_extent_kind":"coastal Genoa–Nice studied reach","approximate_reference_path_km":100,"scenario_range_km":[100,200],"scenario_count":81,"source_url":"https://mrea.sincem.unibo.it/images/reports/2011_Poulain_Aspects_of_the_surface_circulation.pdf","source_locator":"Poulain et al. (2012), Introduction pp. 261–263: NC formation and Italian/French coastal continuation; sections 2.1 and 4, pp. 264–266 and 274–276: surface sampling, Genoa, Imperia, Menton–Nice and current structure.","supporting_sources":[{"url":"https://www.marineregions.org/gazetteer.php?p=details&id=3357","citation":"Marine Regions / VLIZ, MRGID 3357, Ligurian Current; ASFA thesaurus naming entry.","locator":"Place details: Proposed standard, Current, part of Mediterranean Sea; no current endpoint or length geometry supplied.","role":"Naming reference only; does not define this coastal reach or certify Northern Current segment boundaries."},{"url":"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/14/689/2018/","citation":"Berta et al. (2018), Wind-induced variability in the Northern Current (northwestern Mediterranean Sea) as depicted by a multi-platform observing system, Ocean Science 14, 689–710, doi:10.5194/os-14-689-2018.","locator":"Introduction: Liguro-Provencal-Catalan / Northern Current formed in Ligurian Sea and recognizable through Catalan Sea.","role":"Broader parent geography; whole-parent length and regional width summaries are not transferred to this segment."}],"candidate_file":"research/ligurian-reach-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"097cef899d328b72f4069125e1f30d3d5663a9502ca500d74d0ccbeb318a0bba","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","figure":"figures/ligurian-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["MEDI"],"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_C_2","remaining_gates":["Resolve the geographic Ligurian naming convention before whole-segment endpoint admission.","Review source sampling/layer and coastal path with finer bathymetry or compatible current data.","Keep overlapping Northern Current and Ligurian segment lengths separate; do not sum them.","Review local 20 km Menton–Nice profile-band extraction, mixed surface support and remaining Imperia coast-distance limit; no paired whole-current width inferred."],"parent_current_id":"northern-mediterranean","parent_scope_note":"The ledger treats Ligurian Current as a Northern Current segment. This studied reach overlaps the broader current geography; do not add its length to the parent or count it as an independent parallel flow.","ordering_sensitivity":null},{"id":"redsox-southern-plume-reach-reference-path-candidate","current_id":"red-sea-saline-overflow","name":"Red Sea saline overflow - southern plume reference reach","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","comparison_group":"osw_studied_reach_routes","scope":"Declared southern descending-p