ema_eligible":false,"reason":"Winter coastal branch and June-July southern limb have different source-defined spatial scopes; their nominal lengths or scenario bounds do not define annual whole-current extrema."}},{"id":"davidson-historical-winter","current_id":"davidson","phase_label":"October-March (1978 regional summary)","flow_direction":"northward","calendar_months":[10,11,12,1,2,3],"route_candidate_file":"research/davidson-winter-reference-path-candidate.json","route_candidate_sha256":"ac2db281859e27e8903fb224f3fdde35b36f010ab111240e2a2c78e3c5a26609","geometry_role":"osw_editorial_reference_route","width_measurement_ids":["davidson-historical-winter-width"],"width_support_role":"regional_source_context_not_uniform_route_width","width_scope_note":"Approximate 64 km is historical California-Oregon regional context; it is not applied uniformly to the editorial route or used as an occupied footprint.","time_convention":"October-March California-Oregon regional seasonal description in the February 1978 report; strongest flow described in January. Historical summary, not a dated trajectory, current-year observation or modern monthly climatology.","layer":"Seasonal northward surface-current regional context; not the separately described California Undercurrent below 200 m or a reconstructed velocity axis.","source_url":"https://waves-vagues.dfo-mpo.gc.ca/library-bibliotheque/40591190_v2.pdf","source_locator":"Appendix II section II.1, printed II-1 to II-2 / PDF pages 12-13: northward seasonal surface strip along California and Oregon from October to March; Vancouver Island penetration is conditional.","entity_id":"current:davidson","label":"Davidson Current — October-March (1978 regional summary)","status":"editorial_seasonal_route_associations_not_canonical","seasonal_inventory_file":"research/ocean-current-seasonal-route-frames.json","seasonal_inventory_sha256":"5e2bbbcf1aa91253b8ca7d114765364640f62390533af513f205764af63e4422","coordinates_lon_lat":[[-121.1,35],[-1