 Figure3 caption. Exact occupation days and annual coverage unavailable.","boundary_rule":"Author reports band less than200 km wide. No numeric edge cutoff or geographic edge pair supplied; peak/sampled velocities are context only.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1175/1520-0485(1995)025<0077:TSPC>2.0.CO;2","source_citation":"Stramma, L., R.G. Peterson and M. Tomczak (1995), The South Pacific Current, Journal of Physical Oceanography25,77-91.","source_locator":"Original p82 right column; Table1(d) p79, Table2(d) p83 and Figure3/caption p84. Rejected illustrative100 km assumption: p89.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-17","source_evidence_kind":"published_original_scan_reviewed_relative_geostrophic_band_constraint","extraction_method":"Source qualifier and context transcribed after visual review of original pages. No source curve or edge digitization.","whole_current_representative":false,"width_rank_eligible":false,"full_width_inference_eligible":false,"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"seasonal_playback_eligible":false,"is_confidence_interval":false,"phase_label":"Baldrige enhanced eastward band / March 1990","phase_kind":"month_dated_width_constraint","observed_period":null,"calendar_months":null,"fixed_layer_bounds_m":null,"uncertainty_km":null,"source_quality_note":"Original15-page scan retained unchanged and ignored. Full field curves, edge coordinates and width uncertainty have not been digitized or inferred. Frontal bracket differs from velocity width.","remaining_gates":["Recover author boundary definition and exact evaluation depth before paired physical edges.","Acquire compatible repeated sections before seasonal widths or annual extrema.","Independent scientific admission."],"original_regional_context":{"source_quote":"less than 200 km wide","source_section":"d / RV Baldrige","observed_month":"1990-03","nominal_section_longitude_degrees_east":-170,"front_table_longitude_degrees_east":-170.6,"front_station_latitudes_degrees_north":[-43.5,-42.5],"front_bracket_is_width_edges":false,"relative_geostrophic_reference":{"potential_density_symbol":"sigma_2","value_kg_m3":36.75,"source_reference_depth_range_m":[1800,1840],"reference_is_width_layer":false},"source_velocity_context":{"surface_peak_cm_s":7,"near_500m_cm_s":4,"velocities_are_width_cutoffs":false},"field_plot_depth_context_m":[0,1000],"field_plot_context_is_uniform_width_layer":false,"illustrative_transport_width_km":100,"illustrative_transport_width_is_observation":false,"axis_to_ACC_separation_km":{"operator":"gt","value":500,"is_current_width":false},"display_method_note":"One reported less-than band constraint; representative width, lower bound, numerical uncertainty, mapped edges and annual extrema remain unknown. March 1990 dates the observation; 1995 is publication. The 100 km transport assumption and greater-than-500 km separation from ACC flow are distinct contextual values.","display_aria_label":"South Pacific Current: the authors report an enhanced eastward band less than 200 km wide near nominal 170 W in March 1990. Relative geostrophic reference sigma2=36.75 kg/m3 at 1800-1840 m. Representative width, exact days, lower bound and error unknown. No 200 km point, zero-to-200 interval, geographic width band or annual range.","display_caption":"March 1990 / Baldrige section d near nominal 170 W. Source-reported constraint for an enhanced eastward relative-geostrophic band; representative width and paired edges unknown."},"reported_width_constraint":{"kind":"author_reported_dated_less_than","operator":"lt","reference_scale_km":200,"source_notation":"<200 km","is_rigorous_upper_bound":false,"representative_width_km":null,"lower_bound_km":null,"numerical_uncertainty_km":null},"time_precision":"month","observed_month":"1990-03"},"remaining_scientific_gates":["Recover author boundary definition and exact evaluation depth before paired physical edges.","Acquire compatible repeated sections before seasonal widths or annual extrema.","Independent scientific admission."]}},{"id":"diagnostic:south-atlantic-secondary-band","label":"South Atlantic October 1983 southern component breadth","entity_id":"current:south-atlantic","current_id":"south-atlantic","status":"source_reviewed_local_component_not_whole_current_width","rank_eligible":false,"source_file":"research/south-atlantic-stramma-1990-secondary-band-scope-audit.json","source_file_sha256":"c4e7239d16a4c92089b1c2040089026ac5c2816f5de2d60b86ab3f22e83534ed","source_json":"{\n  \"schema\": \"osw.south-atlantic-secondary-band-scope-audit.v1\",\n  \"status\": \"source_reviewed_local_component_not_whole_current_width\",\n  \"current_id\": \"south-atlantic\",\n  \"source_document_file\": \"research/source-data/stramma-south-atlantic-1990/journal-article.pdf\",\n  \"source_document_sha256\": \"f8a926976c10b79227eabbfb28e1d30ae0fe97a87deab2875dfe0abe22af2716\",\n  \"source_pages\": 14,\n  \"acquisition_file\": \"research/source-data/stramma-south-atlantic-1990/acquisition.json\",\n  \"acquisition_sha256\": \"4cd5edc3bde7917fad14b48efcb4d73e45511906026b54a1a9502d8509c7953c\",\n  \"protocol_file\": \"plans/south-atlantic-secondary-band-width-protocol-v1.md\",\n  \"protocol_sha256\": \"277598941c84c9366cf4499a3f315ef06dcef36f5456dd7768c6aab8e0eeb3aa\",\n  \"figure_file\": \"figures/south-atlantic-stramma-1983-secondary-band.svg\",\n  \"figure_sha256\": \"520d58dc2ae2bb2e9c217384e3f916ebf44763c6f09a10f1cb316d5faea8f521\",\n  \"source_review\": {\n    \"method\": \"Visual original page review; OCR for discovery only\",\n    \"publication_pages\": [\n      851,\n      853,\n      854,\n      855\n    ],\n    \"source_curves_digitized\": false,\n    \"source_pdf_is_image_scan\": true\n  },\n  \"measurement\": {\n    \"id\": \"south-atlantic-stramma-1983-10-southern-band-width\",\n    \"current_id\": \"south-atlantic\",\n    \"name\": \"South Atlantic Current\",\n    \"status\": \"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical\",\n    \"measurement_type\": \"published_month_relative_geostrophic_subcomponent_band_width\",\n    \"width_metric\": \"author_reported_secondary_geostrophic_band_breadth\",\n    \"width_metric_label\": \"Southern component band breadth; total SAC width unknown\",\n    \"approximate_width_km\": 200,\n    \"width_range_km\": null,\n    \"range_kind\": null,\n    \"range_interpretation\": \"Nominal source-reported local band breadth; no distribution, confidence interval, seasonal range or whole-current width.\",\n    \"geographic_scope\": \"Knorr Ajax Leg1 section k at1 E, October1983; band south of primary surface Subtropical Front. Secondary core near39-40 S, not width endpoints.\",\n    \"section_geometry\": null,\n    \"section_orientation\": \"Meridional hydrographic section. Source-reported band breadth; no diagnosed local flow-normal axis or paired geographic edges.\",\n    \"layer\": \"Relative-geostrophic southern component band; Figure5d upper1000 m field and transport context. Exact width evaluation depth unresolved; no uniform depth slab.\",\n    \"time_convention\": \"October1983, Table1(k). Exact occupation days unknown;1990 is publication, not observation.\",\n    \"boundary_rule\": \"Source describes a200-km-wide band south of the primary surface front. No explicit numeric velocity edge rule or paired width coordinates. Secondary-core position and offset are separate.\",\n    \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1175/1520-0485(1990)020<0846:TSAC>2.0.CO;2\",\n    \"source_citation\": \"Stramma,L. and R.G.Peterson (1990), The South Atlantic Current, Journal of Physical Oceanography20,846-859.\",\n    \"source_locator\": \"Original p854 right column; Table1(k) p851, Table2(k) p853, Figure5/caption p855.\",\n    \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-17\",\n    \"source_evidence_kind\": \"published_original_scan_reviewed_local_subcomponent_band_breadth\",\n    \"extraction_method\": \"Visual original page review; nominal breadth transcribed. No source curve, flow boundary or uncertainty digitized.\",\n    \"whole_current_representative\": false,\n    \"width_rank_eligible\": false,\n    \"full_width_inference_eligible\": false,\n    \"annual_extrema_eligible\": false,\n    \"seasonal_playback_eligible\": false,\n    \"is_confidence_interval\": false,\n    \"phase_label\": \"Southern component band / October 1983\",\n    \"phase_kind\": \"month_dated_subcomponent_band_breadth\",\n    \"observed_period\": null,\n    \"observed_month\": \"1983-10\",\n    \"time_precision\": \"month\",\n    \"calendar_months\": null,\n    \"fixed_layer_bounds_m\": null,\n    \"uncertainty_km\": null,\n    \"source_quality_note\": \"One historical band component; primary front carries additional SAC flow. Total-current breadth and secondary-core diameter remain unresolved.\",\n    \"remaining_gates\": [\n      \"Recover paired geographic width edges and explicit boundary criterion.\",\n      \"Recover exact width evaluation depth and occupation days.\",\n      \"Acquire compatible repeated same-component sections before annual or seasonal comparison.\"\n    ],\n    \"original_regional_context\": {\n      \"description_kind\": \"historical_sac_southern_component_band\",\n      \"source_section\": \"k / Knorr Ajax Cruise Leg1\",\n      \"observed_month\": \"1983-10\",\n      \"component_role\": \"Southern SAC transport band south of the primary surface Subtropical Front; excludes the primary-front contribution.\",\n      \"source_reported_band_breadth_km\": 200,\n      \"total_current_width_km\": null,\n      \"secondary_core_width_km\": null,\n      \"nominal_section_longitude_degrees_east\": 1,\n      \"primary_surface_front_station_latitudes_degrees_north\": [\n        -38,\n        -37\n      ],\n      \"secondary_core_latitudes_degrees_north\": [\n        -40,\n        -39\n      ],\n      \"source_approximate_core_offset_south_of_primary_front_km\": 200,\n      \"core_offset_is_width\": false,\n      \"front_or_core_bracket_is_width_edges\": false,\n      \"relative_geostrophic_reference\": {\n        \"potential_density_symbol\": \"sigma_4\",\n        \"value_kg_m3\": 45.87,\n        \"source_reference_depth_range_m\": [\n          3470,\n          3560\n        ],\n        \"reference_is_width_layer\": false\n      },\n      \"field_plot_depth_context_m\": [\n        0,\n        1000\n      ],\n      \"field_plot_context_is_uniform_width_layer\": false,\n      \"transport_context\": {\n        \"source_rounded_southern_band_sv\": 8,\n        \"source_rounded_sac_sv\": 17,\n        \"table2_southern_band_sv\": 8.3,\n        \"table2_at_front_sv\": 8.8,\n        \"table2_north_of_front_sv\": -1.4,\n        \"integration_depth_range_m\": [\n          0,\n          1000\n        ],\n        \"transport_is_width_uncertainty\": false,\n        \"width_derived_from_transport\": false\n      },\n      \"display_title\": \"Historical southern component band\",\n      \"display_aria_label\": \"South Atlantic Current: authors report a200 km wide southern component band at1 E in October1983. The primary front carries additional SAC flow; total SAC width and secondary-core diameter unknown. Relative geostrophic reference sigma4=45.87 kg/m3 at3470-3560 m. Width depth, edges, exact days and error unknown; no annual range.\",\n      \"display_caption\": \"October 1983 / Knorr section k at 1 E. Source-reported southern component band breadth; additional SAC flow crosses the primary front. Total-current width unknown.\",\n      \"display_method_note\": \"200 km describes the southern band, not the entire SAC or the diameter of its secondary core. The similarly sized core offset is distinct. Width-evaluation depth, edge cutoff, paired geographic boundaries and numerical error remain unknown. No annual or seasonal inference.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"remaining_scientific_gates\": [\n    \"Recover paired geographic width edges and explicit boundary criterion.\",\n    \"Recover exact width evaluation depth and occupation days.\",\n    \"Acquire compatible repeated same-component sections