latitudes fail the264-month completeness rule. The northern mode peaks at the retained support edge; no missing northern edge or full source-domain shape is inferred.","context_band_membership_rule":"Implementation clarification: WJ includes both endpoints; MC excludes its lower endpoint; SECC excludes its upper endpoint. Shared point membership is never counted twice. These are classification contexts, not current boundaries."},"research_evidence":{"current_id":"indian-south-equatorial-countercurrent","label":"Indian South Equatorial Countercurrent","diagnostic_id":"diagnostic:current-research:indian-south-equatorial-countercurrent","title":"Seasonal patterns: classification evidence","finding":"Two neighboring OSCAR columns over 1995–2016 show similar leading statistical patterns. The southern pattern peaks near 5°S, with an April maximum in its monthly coefficient climatology. This does not verify a named current or its physical edges.","facts":[{"label":"Pattern-current association","value":"Not independently verified"},{"label":"Current width","value":"Unknown"},{"label":"Annual width range","value":"Unknown"},{"label":"Source coverage","value":"Two native columns · 1995–2016"}],"notes":["Five northern latitudes fail complete monthly support. Missing observations are not land or zero flow; the northern pattern peaks at the retained data edge.","Latitude bands are paper classification context, not current boundaries. Principal-component coefficients are not local current speeds.","Three latitude windows and both native columns remain separate. Similarity within one product is not independent validation or a confidence interval.","Exact author domain/weighting/code were unavailable; this experiment is not an exact reproduction."],"next_evidence":"Independent flow association and comparable transverse velocity sections before physical-width admission.","figure_file":"figures/indian-secc-eof-feasibility.svg","figure_alt":"Three statistical loading patterns and mont